window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-22"] = [{"id":1,"rawContent":"# 第 09 章　對不上的記憶\n\n九月二十三號，星期日。早上六點半。\n\n林澈被一連串訊息聲吵醒。\n\n群組裡，阿達連傳了五則：「鏡子開了！！」「七點就開了！」「而且超亮！！」「你們快來！！」「我在學校了！！」\n\n林澈從床上坐起來。今天是……第七天。\n\n他換好衣服，抓起那支藍色的鉛筆塞進口袋，騎上腳踏車。\n\n清晨的海聲國小，安靜得像另一個世界。\n\n校門口的小七招牌，已經連續好幾分鐘保持「海聲書店」的藍色了。它像一台壞掉的電視，卡在兩個頻道之間。\n\n林澈在招牌下停了幾秒，才繼續騎。\n\n舊禮堂前，晴晴和阿達已經到了。\n\n「你終於來了！」阿達揮手，「快看！」\n\n鏡子大開著。銀白色的光比以前任何一天都亮，像有人把一整片月光裝進了鏡子裡。\n\n牆上的裂紋，也變多了。細細的光紋像樹枝一樣，從鏡框往外伸，爬滿了半面牆。\n\n「最後一天。」晴晴說，「所有的謎，都要在今天解開。」\n\n就在他們要走進禮堂的時候，林澈看見了一個人。\n\n校門口，站著一個女生。她揹著書包，一動也不動，像在等誰。\n\n是小筠。郭小筠。六年一班最安靜、功課最好的女生。她平常獨來獨往，午餐總是一個人吃，座位在最後一排的角落。\n\n「小筠？」阿達大叫，「你怎麼在學校？」\n\n小筠轉過頭。她的眼睛紅紅的，像整晚沒睡。\n\n「我的記憶……」她的聲音很輕，很抖，「多了一段不屬於我的東西。」\n\n三個人愣住了。\n\n小筠從書包裡拿出一張紙。紙上，她用原子筆密密麻麻地寫滿了字。\n\n「昨天晚上，我忽然『想起來』一件事。」她說，「我記得，我跟一群人一起吃午餐。有人偷夾我的雞腿，有人幫我倒果汁，大家笑成一團。」\n\n「可是，」她的聲音開始發抖，「我從來沒有跟人一起吃過午餐。一個人都沒有。」\n\n她看著他們三個，眼淚在眼眶裡打轉：「那段記憶，好溫暖。溫暖得……像是偷來的。」\n\n林澈的心揪了一下。\n\n他太懂了。那種「別人的快樂」闖進自己腦海的感覺。\n\n「那不是偷來的。」晴晴說，語氣難得溫柔，「那是 B 世界的你的記憶。」\n\n小筠瞪大眼睛。\n\n「B 世界……？真的有另一個我？」\n\n「有。」林澈點頭，「而且，」他頓了一下，「在那個世界，你每天中午，都跟一群人一起吃飯。」\n\n小筠張了張嘴，什麼都沒說出來。\n\n晴晴看了她一眼：「你要跟我們一起進去嗎？親眼看看另一個你。」\n\n小筠低下頭。過了好久，她點了點頭。\n\n四個人走進禮堂。\n\n鏡子裡，B 世界的舊禮堂同樣大開著。對面已經站滿了人。\n\n「你們遲到了！」小陽站在最前面，雙手叉腰，聲音大得嚇人，「我們六點就起來了！」\n\n達哥笑他：「明明是你五點就把我們全部吵醒。」\n\n四個 A 世界的人穿過鏡子。\n\n小筠是最後一個。\n\n她的腳踏進 B 世界的瞬間，整個人輕輕顫了一下。\n\n「歡迎光臨。」B 晴晴笑著對她說。然後她轉頭朝後面喊：「小筠！快過來！」\n\n一個女生從人群裡擠出來。\n\n齊耳短髮，圓圓的眼鏡，書包側邊插著一本厚厚的小說。\n\n是 B 世界的小筠。\n\n兩個小筠，面對面。\n\n一樣的眼睛，一樣的鼻子，一樣的緊張表情。\n\n可是 B 小筠的背後，站著一群人。\n\n「那是誰啊？」B 小筠的朋友們湊過來，好奇地打量，「哇，小筠變成兩個了！」「好酷喔！」「哪個才是真的小筠？」\n\n「都是真的啦！」B 小筠推了推朋友，笑了起來。\n\n她笑得那麼自然。好像「有朋友在旁邊」，是世界上最理所當然的事。\n\nA 小筠看著她，忽然說：「你……每天中午，都有人陪你吃飯嗎？」\n\nB 小筠愣了一下：「對啊。怎麼了嗎？」\n\n「沒有。」A 小筠低下頭，聲音很小，「我只是……覺得很好。」\n\n氣氛安靜了一秒。\n\nB 小筠的朋友之一，一個綁馬尾的女生，忽然走過來，拉住 A 小筠的手：「走啊，等一下跟我們一起吃午餐！反正你們中午以前都會在這裡吧？」\n\nA 小筠整個人僵住。\n\n「……好。」她說。聲音小得像蚊子。\n\n可是林澈看到，她的嘴角，很小很小地，往上彎了一下。\n\n會議開始了。\n\n兩班的人聚在 B 世界的草坪上，圍成一個大圓圈。\n\n晴晴和 B 晴晴各自拿出筆記本。兩本筆記本攤在一起，像兩片拼圖。\n\n「我們先比對兩邊的差異。」晴晴說。\n\n一項一項列出來：\n\n「第一，書店。A 世界是小七，B 世界是海聲書店。」\n\n「第二，溜滑梯。A 世界沒有，B 世界有。」\n\n「第三，農場。A 世界是水泥地，B 世界有班級農場。」\n\n「第四，班長。A 世界是予晴，B 世界是小陽。」\n\n「第五，佈告欄。A 世界是公布欄，B 世界貼滿安安的畫。」\n\n「第六，阿達的綽號。A 世界沒有綽號，B 世界被叫達哥。」\n\n「第七……」B 晴晴接著說，「小筠的朋友。我們這邊的小筠，有一群死黨。」\n\n所有人都看向 A 小筠。\n\n她低著頭，耳朵紅紅的。\n\n晴晴把筆記本閤上，環顧所有人：「你們有沒有發現？這些差異，都不是隨機的。」\n\n「不是隨機的？」阿達問。\n\n「嗯。」小筠忽然開口。她的聲音還是很小，可是很清楚，「書店、溜滑梯、農場、佈告欄……這些是『東西』。但班長、綽號、朋友、被貼出來的畫……這些，都跟一件事有關。」\n\n「什麼事？」小陽湊過來。\n\n「班級怎麼對待班上的每一個人。」小筠說，「在 B 世界，有人被鼓勵、有人被看見、有人有朋友。在 A 世界……」\n\n她沒有說下去。\n\n可是每個人都懂了。\n\n晴晴的眼睛亮起來：「所以，兩個世界從某個時刻開始，『對待人的方式』整個分岔了。」\n\n「只要能找到那個時刻……」B 晴晴接著說。\n\n「就能知道，這一切是從哪裡開始的。」林澈說完了這句。\n\n風吹過草坪，把大家的頭髮吹亂。\n\n「好！」小陽站起來，拳頭往天空一舉，「兩班聯合調查，正式開始！」\n\n「喔——！」孩子們一起大喊。\n\n忽然，B 世界那邊，有人尖叫。\n\n「溜滑梯！」\n\n所有人回頭。\n\n草坪邊的溜滑梯，閃了一下。就像電視機換台，藍色的溜滑梯，一瞬間變成了半透明的影子，然後又恢復原狀。\n\nB 世界的孩子們，臉色全白了。\n\n「覆蓋……變快了。」晴晴喃喃。\n\n林澈正要說話，忽然看到了一件事。\n\n達哥站在溜滑梯旁邊，正在安撫大家。陽光很大，每個人的影子都清清楚楚地躺在地上。\n\n只有達哥的腳下，沒有影子。\n\n一瞬間。然後，影子又回來了。\n\n林澈揉了揉眼睛。\n\n他沒有告訴任何人。\n\n可是他的心臟，跳得比早上的鬧鐘還大聲。\n\n十點半。四個人準備回 A 世界。\n\n「十一點前要回去。」晴晴看著手錶，「三小時的限制。」\n\n小筠站在鏡子前，回頭看了一眼。\n\nB 小筠和她的朋友們，正站在草坪上朝她揮手。\n\n「等一下見！」綁馬尾的女生大喊，「記得跟我們吃午餐！」\n\n小筠沒有回答。她只是用力地點了一下頭，然後，一腳踏進鏡子裡。\n\n回到 A 世界，四個人走出禮堂。\n\n林澈回頭看了一眼。牆上的裂紋，比剛才又多了一條。\n\n一條新的、發著光的裂紋，正往操場的方向爬去。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 09 — Memories That Don't Match\n\nSeptember 23rd, Sunday. 6:30 in the morning.\n\nLin Che was woken by a rapid burst of message notifications.\n\nIn the group chat, A-Da had sent five messages in a row: \"The mirror's open!!\" \"It opened at seven!\" \"And it's super bright!!\" \"Hurry up!!\" \"I'm already at school!!\"\n\nLin Che sat up in bed. Today was... the seventh day.\n\nHe got dressed, grabbed the blue pencil and stuffed it into his pocket, and hopped on his bike.\n\nHaisheng Elementary in the early morning was quiet, like another world itself.\n\nThe 7-Eleven sign by the school gate had now been holding its \"Haisheng Bookstore\" blue for several minutes straight. It was like a broken TV, stuck between two channels.\n\nLin Che paused under the sign for a few seconds before pedaling on.\n\nIn front of the old auditorium, Ching-Ching and A-Da had already arrived.\n\n\"You finally made it!\" A-Da waved. \"Look, quick!\"\n\nThe mirror was wide open. The silvery-white light was brighter than any day before, as if someone had poured an entire sheet of moonlight into the mirror.\n\nThe cracks on the wall had multiplied too. Thin glowing lines stretched out from the mirror frame like branches, crawling across half the wall.\n\n\"The last day,\" Ching-Ching said. \"Every mystery has to be solved today.\"\n\nJust as they were about to enter the auditorium, Lin Che spotted someone.\n\nStanding at the school gate was a girl. Backpack on, completely still, as if waiting for someone.\n\nIt was Hsiao-Yun. Kuo Hsiao-Yun. The quietest and smartest girl in Class 6-1. She usually kept to herself, always ate lunch alone, and sat in the corner of the last row.\n\n\"Hsiao-Yun?\" A-Da shouted. \"What are you doing at school?\"\n\nHsiao-Yun turned. Her eyes were red, as if she hadn't slept all night.\n\n\"My memory...\" her voice was soft and trembling, \"has gained a piece that doesn't belong to me.\"\n\nThe three of them froze.\n\nHsiao-Yun pulled a sheet of paper from her backpack. It was densely covered in her ballpoint handwriting.\n\n\"Last night, I suddenly 'remembered' something,\" she said. \"I remember eating lunch with a group of people. Someone stole a piece of my chicken leg, someone poured juice for me, everyone laughed together.\"\n\n\"But,\" her voice began to shake, \"I have never eaten lunch with anyone. Not once.\"\n\nShe looked at the three of them, tears welling in her eyes: \"That memory was so warm. So warm... it felt like it was stolen.\"\n\nLin Che's heart clenched.\n\nHe understood it all too well. That feeling of someone else's happiness barging into your own mind.\n\n\"It wasn't stolen,\" Ching-Ching said, her tone uncharacteristically gentle. \"That's the memory of the you in World B.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun's eyes went wide.\n\n\"World B...? There really is another me?\"\n\n\"There is.\" Lin Che nodded. \"And,\" he paused, \"in that world, you eat lunch with a group of people every day at noon.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun opened her mouth, but nothing came out.\n\nChing-Ching glanced at her: \"Do you want to come in with us? To see the other you with your own eyes.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun lowered her head. After a long while, she nodded.\n\nThe four of them walked into the auditorium.\n\nIn the mirror, the old auditorium of World B was wide open too. The other side was already crowded with people.\n\n\"You're late!\" Xiao-Yang stood at the front, hands on his hips, his voice alarmingly loud. \"We've been up since six!\"\n\nDa-ge laughed at him: \"You're the one who woke all of us up at five.\"\n\nThe four from World A passed through the mirror.\n\nHsiao-Yun was the last one.\n\nThe moment her foot stepped into World B, her whole body shivered slightly.\n\n\"Welcome.\" B Ching-Ching smiled at her. Then she turned and called behind: \"Hsiao-Yun! Come here, quick!\"\n\nA girl squeezed out of the crowd.\n\nEar-length hair, round glasses, a thick novel tucked into the side pocket of her backpack.\n\nIt was the Hsiao-Yun of World B.\n\nTwo Hsiao-Yuns, face to face.\n\nSame eyes, same nose, same nervous expression.\n\nBut behind B Hsiao-Yun stood a whole group of people.\n\n\"Who's that?\" B Hsiao-Yun's friends crowded over, sizing her up curiously. \"Whoa, there are two Hsiao-Yuns now!\" \"So cool!\" \"Which one is the real one?\"\n\n\"They're both real!\" B Hsiao-Yun nudged her friends and laughed.\n\nShe laughed so naturally, as if having friends by her side was the most obvious thing in the world.\n\nA Hsiao-Yun looked at her and suddenly asked: \"Do you... always have people eating lunch with you, every day at noon?\"\n\nB Hsiao-Yun blinked: \"Of course. Why?\"\n\n\"Nothing.\" A Hsiao-Yun lowered her head, her voice tiny. \"I just... think that's really nice.\"\n\nThe atmosphere went quiet for a second.\n\nOne of B Hsiao-Yun's friends, a girl with a ponytail, suddenly walked over and took A Hsiao-Yun's hand: \"Come on, eat lunch with us later! You guys will be here until noon anyway, right?\"\n\nA Hsiao-Yun froze completely.\n\n\"...Okay,\" she said. Her voice was as small as a mosquito's.\n\nBut Lin Che saw the corner of her mouth curve upward, just a tiny, tiny bit.\n\nThe meeting began.\n\nThe two classes gathered on the World B lawn, sitting in one big circle.\n\nChing-Ching and B Ching-Ching each took out their notebooks. The two notebooks lay open together, like two pieces of a puzzle.\n\n\"First, let's compare the differences between the two sides,\" Ching-Ching said.\n\nShe listed them one by one:\n\n\"One, the bookstore. World A has a 7-Eleven; World B has Haisheng Bookstore.\"\n\n\"Two, the slide. World A doesn't have one; World B does.\"\n\n\"Three, the farm. World A has a concrete lot; World B has a class farm.\"\n\n\"Four, the class monitor. In World A it's Yu-Ching; in World B it's Xiao-Yang.\"\n\n\"Five, the bulletin board. World A has a notice board; World B has An-An's drawings all over it.\"\n\n\"Six, A-Da's nickname. World A has none; in World B he's called Da-ge.\"\n\n\"Seven...\" B Ching-Ching picked it up. \"Hsiao-Yun's friends. Over here, our Hsiao-Yun has a group of best friends.\"\n\nEveryone turned to look at A Hsiao-Yun.\n\nShe kept her head down, ears reddening.\n\nChing-Ching closed her notebook and looked around at everyone: \"Have you noticed? None of these differences are random.\"\n\n\"Not random?\" A-Da asked.\n\n\"Mm.\" Hsiao-Yun suddenly spoke. Her voice was still small, but very clear. \"The bookstore, the slide, the farm, the bulletin board... those are 'things.' But the monitor, the nickname, the friends, the drawings on display... those all connect to one thing.\"\n\n\"What thing?\" Xiao-Yang leaned in.\n\n\"How the class treats each and every person in it,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"In World B, people are encouraged, people are seen, people have friends. In World A...\"\n\nShe didn't finish the sentence.\n\nBut everyone understood.\n\nChing-Ching's eyes lit up: \"So starting from some moment, the two worlds' 'way of treating people' completely split apart.\"\n\n\"If we can find that moment...\" B Ching-Ching continued.\n\n\"...then we'll know where all of this began,\" Lin Che finished.\n\nThe wind swept across the lawn, tousling everyone's hair.\n\n\"Alright!\" Xiao-Yang stood up and raised a fist to the sky. \"The Two-Class Joint Investigation officially begins!\"\n\n\"Yay—!\" all the children shouted together.\n\nSuddenly, from the World B side, someone screamed.\n\n\"The slide!\"\n\nEveryone turned.\n\nThe slide by the lawn flickered. Like a TV changing channels, the blue slide became a translucent shadow for an instant, then snapped back to normal.\n\nThe World B children all went pale.\n\n\"The overwriting... is speeding up,\" Ching-Ching murmured.\n\nJust as Lin Che was about to speak, he saw something.\n\nDa-ge stood beside the slide, comforting everyone. The sun was bright, and everyone's shadow lay clear on the ground.\n\nOnly at Da-ge's feet, there was no shadow.\n\nFor an instant. Then the shadow came back.\n\nLin Che rubbed his eyes.\n\nHe didn't tell anyone.\n\nBut his heart was pounding louder than his morning alarm.\n\n10:30. The four of them got ready to return to World A.\n\n\"We have to be back before eleven,\" Ching-Ching checked her watch. \"The three-hour limit.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun stood before the mirror and glanced back.\n\nB Hsiao-Yun and her friends were standing on the lawn, waving at her.\n\n\"See you in a bit!\" the ponytail girl shouted. \"Don't forget to eat lunch with us!\"\n\nHsiao-Yun didn't answer. She just nodded firmly once, then stepped into the mirror.\n\nBack in World A, the four of them walked out of the auditorium.\n\nLin Che looked back. The cracks on the wall had gained one more line.\n\nA new, glowing crack was crawling toward the playground.\n"},{"id":2,"rawContent":"# 第 10 章　阿達的兩種人生\n\n中午十二點。四個 A 世界的人再次穿過鏡子。\n\nB 世界的校園，飄著午餐的香味。\n\n「就等你們了！」小陽在校門口揮手，「今天吃咖哩！」\n\n草坪上，B 世界的孩子們鋪了一大片野餐墊，便當盒排成一列。\n\n小筠站在人群外，抓著書包帶子，猶豫著不敢過去。\n\n「小筠！這裡！」綁馬尾的女生揮手。\n\nA 小筠一步一步走過去，坐在 B 小筠身邊。\n\n便當一盒一盒打開。B 小筠的朋友們搶著幫她夾菜、倒果汁。\n\n「你試試看這個！」「這是我媽媽做的！」「啊，雞腿是我的！」\n\nA 小筠捧著自己的便當，夾起一小口飯，慢慢放進嘴裡。\n\n她忽然低下頭。肩膀輕輕地抖。\n\n「你怎麼了？」B 小筠嚇了一跳。\n\n「沒有。」A 小筠的聲音悶悶的，「只是……原來大家一起吃飯，是這種感覺。」\n\n她抬起頭。眼睛濕濕的，可是在笑。\n\n「好好吃。」她說。\n\n大家都笑了。\n\n不遠處，阿達一個人坐著，咬著麵包，不知道在想什麼。\n\n林澈走過去，坐在他旁邊。\n\n「你不吃便當？」林澈問。\n\n「我媽早上沒空，只塞了一百塊。」阿達聳肩，「反正我也不太餓。」\n\n他看著草坪上的人群，忽然說：「喂，你覺不覺得，達哥真的很厲害？」\n\n「很厲害？」\n\n「你看。」阿達用下巴比了比，「剛才小陽說要辦什麼『最後一天的大會』，達哥馬上就把分組、活動、時間表全部想好了。」\n\n草坪上，達哥站在人群中央，手上揮著一張紙，正在大聲分配任務。旁邊的人不停點頭，還有人拿筆記下來。\n\n「在我們班，我也會這樣。」阿達的聲音低了下去，「我也會分組、也會想活動。可是——」\n\n「可是大家只會笑。」他笑了，笑得很難看，「說：阿達又在耍寶了。」\n\n林澈張了張嘴，卻不知道該說什麼。\n\n因為他知道，阿達說的是真的。\n\n「你知道嗎？」阿達忽然說，「其實我不是開玩笑。」\n\n「什麼？」\n\n「鏡子的事。」阿達看著遠方，「我們發現鏡子之前，我就看過你。」\n\n林澈愣住。\n\n「上禮拜有一天，我放學後去禮堂後面撿彈珠，看到你在舊禮堂裡，跟一個長得跟你一模一樣的人講話。」\n\n「我以為是鬼，嚇得跑掉。後來想想，那說不定就是……」\n\n「就是鏡子裡的世界。」林澈接話，聲音很輕。\n\n「嗯。」阿達抓抓頭，「所以我一直都知道，你不是普通的安靜鬼。你只是……還沒被看見。」\n\n林澈的心裡，像被什麼輕輕撞了一下。\n\n「你也不是普通的小丑。」林澈說。\n\n阿達轉頭看他。\n\n「我是說，」林澈結結巴巴，「你的點子，其實都很好。只是……我們班的人，太習慣把你當成搞笑的阿達了。」\n\n阿達愣愣地看著他，忽然「噗」一聲笑出來。\n\n「謝啦。」他搥了林澈一下，「你這傢伙，不講話則已，一講就戳中要害。」\n\n就在這時，達哥朝他們走了過來。\n\n「喂，兩個躲在這裡幹嘛？」達哥一屁股坐下來，「快點，我需要人手。」\n\n他攤開手裡的紙，上面畫滿了亂七八槽的流程圖。\n\n「最後一天，我們想辦一個『兩個世界的同學會』。」達哥眼睛發亮，「兩班一起玩遊戲、一起唱歌、交換禮物。你們也要一起！」\n\n「聽起來很讚耶！」阿達脫口而出，隨即又縮了縮脖子，「可是……你們聽我的意見幹嘛？」\n\n「幹嘛不聽？」達哥挑眉，「你跟我有同一顆腦袋耶。你的點子，就是我的點子。」\n\n阿達愣住了。\n\n「我只是運氣好，」達哥聳聳肩，「遇到了一群願意聽我講話的人。就醬。」\n\n「就醬」兩個字，像一顆小石子，掉進阿達心裡，泛起一圈一圈的波紋。\n\n「那……」阿達深吸一口氣，忽然站起來，「我覺得，同學會可以加一個『兩個世界交換卡片』的活動！」\n\n達哥的眼睛亮起來：「交換卡片？你繼續說！」\n\n阿達開始講。一開始還有點結巴，越講越快，手也開始比劃。\n\n達哥認真地聽，聽到重點還會點頭，拿筆記下來。\n\n林澈坐在旁邊，看著這一幕。\n\n他忽然覺得，阿達的肩膀，好像挺起來了一點。\n\n下午一點，B 世界農場邊。\n\n達哥從田裡摘了幾顆草莓，塞到三個人手裡。給阿達的，特別大顆。\n\n「農場長的特權。」達哥眨眼，「我們這邊的草莓，特別甜。」\n\n阿達把草莓放進口袋。他捨不得吃。\n\n「等我回去再吃。」他說。\n\n忽然，農場的方向傳來一陣騷動。\n\n「草莓！草莓不見了！」\n\n大家跑過去。田畦上，幾株草莓……消失了。\n\n不是被拔走。是整株草莓，連土都看不見了。原地只剩下一小塊乾乾淨淨的水泥地。\n\n「覆蓋……」B 晴晴的聲音發抖，「連這裡也開始了。」\n\n孩子們圍著那一小塊水泥地，安靜了下來。\n\n「A 世界那裡，就是一片水泥地。」林澈輕聲說。\n\n所有人抬頭看他。\n\n「所以，這裡正在變成我們那邊。」他說。\n\n「而我們那邊，正在變成這裡。」晴晴接話。\n\n「兩個世界，正在互相吃掉對方。」\n\n沒人說話。海風吹過農場，把僅存的幾株草莓吹得搖晃。\n\n兩點。回程的時間到了。\n\n四個人走到鏡子前。\n\n阿達是倒數第二個進去的。他回頭看了一眼 B 世界。\n\n草坪上，達哥還在跟同學討論同學會。大家圍著他，聽他說話，眼睛發亮。\n\n阿達把手伸進口袋，握住那顆草莓。\n\n草莓涼涼的。可是他的手心，是熱的。\n\n「如果……」他低聲說。\n\n「阿達！」晴晴在鏡子另一邊喊他。\n\n「來了！」\n\n他深吸一口氣，一腳踏進鏡子裡。\n\n那天晚上，阿達坐在書桌前，把那顆草莓放在檯燈下。\n\n草莓很紅，紅得像一顆小小的太陽。\n\n他沒有吃。他就只是看著它。\n\n書桌上，媽媽留了一張便條：「爸爸媽媽今天晚回來，冰箱有便當。」\n\n阿達把便條紙摺成一架小小的紙飛機，放在草莓旁邊。\n\n然後，他在作業本的最後一頁，寫下三個字。\n\n「想留下。」\n\n寫完，他盯著那三個字看了很久。\n\n最後，他把那一頁，輕輕撕了下來。\n\n揉成一團，丟進垃圾桶。\n\n可是那三個字，已經像種子一樣，種進了他的心裡。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 10 — A-Da's Two Lives\n\nTwelve noon. The four from World A passed through the mirror once more.\n\nThe World B campus was filled with the smell of lunch.\n\n\"We've been waiting for you!\" Xiao-Yang waved at the school gate. \"It's curry today!\"\n\nOn the lawn, the World B children had spread out a huge picnic mat, with lunch boxes lined up in a row.\n\nHsiao-Yun stood outside the crowd, clutching her backpack straps, hesitating to go over.\n\n\"Hsiao-Yun! Over here!\" the ponytail girl waved.\n\nA Hsiao-Yun walked over step by step and sat down beside B Hsiao-Yun.\n\nLunch boxes opened one by one. B Hsiao-Yun's friends rushed to put food in her box and pour her juice.\n\n\"Try this!\" \"My mom made this!\" \"Hey, that chicken leg is mine!\"\n\nA Hsiao-Yun held her own lunch box, picked up a small bite of rice, and slowly put it in her mouth.\n\nShe suddenly lowered her head. Her shoulders trembled slightly.\n\n\"What's wrong?\" B Hsiao-Yun was startled.\n\n\"Nothing.\" A Hsiao-Yun's voice was muffled. \"It's just... so this is what it feels like to eat together.\"\n\nShe looked up. Her eyes were wet, but she was smiling.\n\n\"It's so good,\" she said.\n\nEveryone laughed.\n\nNot far away, A-Da sat alone, chewing on a piece of bread, lost in thought.\n\nLin Che walked over and sat down next to him.\n\n\"No lunch box?\" Lin Che asked.\n\n\"Mom didn't have time this morning. She just gave me a hundred bucks.\" A-Da shrugged. \"I'm not that hungry anyway.\"\n\nLooking at the crowd on the lawn, he suddenly said: \"Hey, don't you think Da-ge is really impressive?\"\n\n\"Impressive?\"\n\n\"Look.\" A-Da jutted his chin. \"Just now Xiao-Yang said he wanted to hold some 'last day assembly,' and Da-ge immediately figured out the groups, the activities, the whole schedule.\"\n\nOn the lawn, Da-ge stood at the center of the crowd, waving a sheet of paper and loudly handing out tasks. The kids around him kept nodding, and some were even taking notes.\n\n\"In our class, I'd do the same thing.\" A-Da's voice dropped. \"I'd make the groups too. I'd think up activities too. But—\"\n\n\"But everyone just laughs.\" He smiled, an ugly smile. \"And says: there goes A-Da clowning around again.\"\n\nLin Che opened his mouth, but didn't know what to say.\n\nBecause he knew what A-Da said was true.\n\n\"You know what?\" A-Da suddenly said. \"I actually wasn't joking.\"\n\n\"What?\"\n\n\"About the mirror.\" A-Da looked into the distance. \"I'd seen you before we ever found the mirror.\"\n\nLin Che froze.\n\n\"One day last week, after school, I went behind the auditorium to pick up a marble, and I saw you in the old auditorium, talking to a person who looked exactly like you.\"\n\n\"I thought it was a ghost and ran off scared. Thinking back on it, that was probably...\"\n\n\"The world inside the mirror.\" Lin Che finished, his voice soft.\n\n\"Yeah.\" A-Da scratched his head. \"So I always knew you weren't just some quiet ghost. You're just... someone who hasn't been seen yet.\"\n\nSomething gently bumped into Lin Che's heart.\n\n\"You're not just some clown either,\" Lin Che said.\n\nA-Da turned to look at him.\n\n\"I mean,\" Lin Che stammered, \"your ideas are actually really good. It's just... the kids in our class are too used to treating you as the funny A-Da.\"\n\nA-Da stared at him blankly, then burst out laughing with a \"pfft.\"\n\n\"Thanks.\" He thumped Lin Che on the shoulder. \"Man, you barely talk, but when you do, it hits the spot.\"\n\nJust then, Da-ge walked over toward them.\n\n\"Hey, what are you two doing hiding over here?\" Da-ge plopped down. \"Come on, I need hands.\"\n\nHe spread out the paper in his hand, covered in messy flowcharts.\n\n\"For the last day, we want to hold a 'Two-Worlds Class Reunion.'\" Da-ge's eyes sparkled. \"Both classes play games together, sing together, exchange gifts. You guys have to join in too!\"\n\n\"That sounds awesome!\" A-Da blurted out, then shrank back a little. \"But... why would you listen to my opinions?\"\n\n\"Why wouldn't we?\" Da-ge raised an eyebrow. \"You and I have the same brain. Your ideas are my ideas.\"\n\nA-Da was stunned.\n\n\"I just got lucky,\" Da-ge shrugged. \"I found a group of people willing to listen to me talk. That's all.\"\n\n\"That's all\" — those two words dropped into A-Da's heart like a little pebble, sending out ring after ring of ripples.\n\n\"Then...\" A-Da took a deep breath and suddenly stood up. \"I think the reunion should have a 'Two-Worlds Card Exchange' activity!\"\n\nDa-ge's eyes lit up: \"Card exchange? Go on!\"\n\nA-Da started talking. He stuttered a bit at first, but talked faster and faster, his hands beginning to gesture.\n\nDa-ge listened seriously, nodding at the key points and taking notes.\n\nLin Che sat nearby, watching.\n\nHe suddenly felt that A-Da's shoulders seemed to have straightened a little.\n\nOne o'clock in the afternoon, by the World B farm.\n\nDa-ge picked a few strawberries from the field and pressed them into the three visitors' hands. The one he gave A-Da was especially big.\n\n\"Farm manager's privilege.\" Da-ge winked. \"Our strawberries are extra sweet.\"\n\nA-Da put the strawberry in his pocket. He couldn't bear to eat it.\n\n\"I'll eat it after I get back,\" he said.\n\nSuddenly, a commotion came from the direction of the farm.\n\n\"The strawberries! The strawberries are gone!\"\n\nEveryone ran over. On the field ridges, several strawberry plants... had vanished.\n\nNot pulled out. The whole plants, soil and all, were gone. In their place remained only a small patch of clean, bare cement.\n\n\"The overwriting...\" B Ching-Ching's voice trembled. \"It's starting here too.\"\n\nThe children gathered around that patch of cement and fell quiet.\n\n\"Over in World A, it's all cement there,\" Lin Che said softly.\n\nEveryone looked up at him.\n\n\"So this place is turning into our side,\" he said.\n\n\"And our side is turning into this place,\" Ching-Ching picked up.\n\n\"The two worlds are eating each other.\"\n\nNo one spoke. The sea breeze swept across the farm, swaying the few remaining strawberry plants.\n\nTwo o'clock. Time to head back.\n\nThe four of them walked to the mirror.\n\nA-Da was second-to-last to go in. He glanced back at World B.\n\nOn the lawn, Da-ge was still discussing the reunion with his classmates. They surrounded him, listening, eyes bright.\n\nA-Da reached into his pocket and gripped the strawberry.\n\nThe strawberry was cool. But his palm was warm.\n\n\"If only...\" he whispered.\n\n\"A-Da!\" Ching-Ching called from the other side of the mirror.\n\n\"Coming!\"\n\nHe took a deep breath and stepped into the mirror.\n\nThat night, A-Da sat at his desk and placed the strawberry under his desk lamp.\n\nThe strawberry was very red. Red like a tiny sun.\n\nHe didn't eat it. He just looked at it.\n\nOn the desk lay a note from his mom: \"Dad and Mom will be late tonight. There's a lunch box in the fridge.\"\n\nA-Da folded the note into a tiny paper airplane and placed it beside the strawberry.\n\nThen, on the last page of his homework notebook, he wrote three words.\n\n\"I want to stay.\"\n\nWhen he finished, he stared at those three words for a long, long time.\n\nFinally, he gently tore that page out.\n\nCrumpled it into a ball, and tossed it into the trash can.\n\nBut those three words had already taken root in his heart, like seeds.\n"},{"id":3,"rawContent":"# 第 11 章　天才與死黨\n\n下午兩點十分。調查總部，設在 B 世界的教室裡。\n\n兩班的調查隊分成三組：晴晴和 B 晴晴負責訪談；小陽和阿達負責找場地線索；小筠……一個人，負責把所有線索拼起來。\n\n黑板上，貼滿了便條紙。每一張，都是一條「兩個世界的不同」。\n\n小筠站在黑板前，眼鏡後面的眼睛，專注得嚇人。\n\n她做了一件事：把便條紙，按「時間」重新排。\n\n「大家來幫我回想，」她說，「你最早覺得『這個世界怪怪的』，是什麼時候？」\n\n訪談開始。一個一個問。\n\nB 阿寶：「我記得開學沒多久，林澈就突然變得很紅。大家都說他跑得超快。」\n\nA 小美：「我們這邊的林澈？他一直都很安靜啊。」\n\nB 同學：「開學第三天的體育課，全班都瘋了！林澈跑最後一棒，贏了！」\n\nA 同學：「體育課？第三天？不就選人嗎？沒什麼特別的啊。」\n\n小筠在黑板前來回踱步，把聽到的每一句，寫在便條紙上。\n\n「你們記得的『最早的不同』，全都落在同一個時間。」她推了推眼鏡。\n\n「開學第一週。而且是——體育課。」\n\n「等一下。」晴晴站起來，「你的意思是，在那之前，兩個世界完全一樣？」\n\n「對。」小筠點頭，「如果兩個世界是從某個時刻才分岔，那在那個時刻『之前』，所有人的記憶應該一模一樣。」\n\n「我們只要找到『第一筆不一樣的記憶』，就能找到分岔點。」\n\n小陽拍手：「天才就是天才！」\n\nB 小筠的朋友們也在一旁歡呼：「小筠加油！」「小筠是我們的大腦！」\n\n一個綁馬尾的女生跑出教室，抱了兩瓶果汁回來。\n\n「給！」她把一瓶塞給 B 小筠，另一瓶塞給 A 小筠，「你也是小筠，所以也有份！」\n\nA 小筠接過果汁，愣了好幾秒。\n\n「……謝謝。」她小聲說，耳尖紅紅的。\n\n林澈靠在門邊，看著這一幕，心裡暖暖的。\n\n忽然，他聽見小筠喊他。\n\n「林澈。」小筠走過來，盯著他，「體育課那天，你記不記得自己做了什麼？」\n\n林澈的心跳漏了一拍。\n\n「我……不記得。」\n\n「一點都不記得？」小筠的眼睛，像兩面小鏡子。\n\n林澈搖搖頭。\n\n「可是 B 世界的你，」小筠翻開她的訪談紀錄，「記得清清楚楚。他記得自己接了最後一棒、跑贏、被拋起來。」\n\n「全班二十六個人的記憶都對得上。只有你——」她看著他，「只有你的記憶，是破的。」\n\n教室裡安靜了下來。\n\n林澈忽然覺得，所有人的目光都落在自己身上。\n\n「所以，」小筠的聲音很輕，卻像錘子一樣敲進他的耳朵，「分岔點不但在那天，而且……跟你有關。」\n\n林澈張了張嘴，什麼都說不出來。\n\n他下意識地摸了摸自己的頭。那團霧，好像又薄了一點。\n\n操場。哨子聲。陽光的溫度。\n\n然後，一片空白。\n\n「沒關係。」B 林澈忽然走過來，拍了拍他的肩膀——拍到一半，停住，改成在空中比了一個「加油」的手勢。\n\n「我們會一起想起來的。」他說，「兩個我加起來，總比一個我強吧？」\n\n林澈看著他，慢慢地，點了一下頭。\n\n調查目標確定了。\n\n晴晴在黑板上寫下：「目標：開學第三天，體育課。」\n\n小筠在黑板上補了一句：「第一筆不一樣的記憶。」\n\n所有人看著黑板，忽然都覺得，好像離答案近了一步。\n\n就在這時，教室後面有人驚呼。\n\n「佈告欄！」\n\n大家回頭。\n\n佈告欄上，安安的畫正在一張一張地「換頁」。上一秒還是一幅水彩風景，下一秒變成了……一張普通的通知單。\n\n就像有人在用遙控器，一格一格地切換頻道。\n\n幾秒鐘後，佈告欄恢復原狀。滿滿的畫，一張都沒少。\n\n「覆蓋……連教室裡都進來了。」B 晴晴臉色發白。\n\n孩子們圍著佈告欄，安靜了很久。\n\n最後，小陽開口了。他的聲音，不像平常那麼大。\n\n「我們得再快一點了。」\n\n下午四點。鏡子前。\n\n調查隊準備回 A 世界。今天的進度：鎖定了分岔點。\n\n臨走前，B 小筠塞了一張小紙條給 A 小筠。\n\n紙條上寫著：「明天最後一天，我們一起把謎解開。」\n\n下面畫了兩個牽手的小人，一個綁著馬尾，一個戴著圓眼鏡。\n\nA 小筠把紙條摺好，放進口袋最深的地方。\n\n她回頭看了一眼 B 世界。那群死黨，正朝她揮手。\n\n她沒有揮手。她只是很小聲地，對自己說了一句：\n\n「我也是……有朋友的人了。」\n\n然後，她一腳踏進鏡子裡。\n\n回到 A 世界。四個人走出禮堂。\n\n林澈忽然停下腳步。\n\n「你們先走。我想一個人靜一靜。」\n\n晴晴看了他一眼，點點頭。阿達拍拍他的背。小筠推了推眼鏡。\n\n三個人走了。校園裡，只剩下林澈一個人。\n\n他走到操場邊，蹲下來，摸著紅色跑道。\n\n夕陽把操場染成橘色。海風一陣一陣地吹。\n\n「開學第三天……」他喃喃。\n\n他想用力去想。那天的畫面，像霧裡的影子，一閃一閃。\n\n哨子聲。\n\n太陽。\n\n一群低頭的人。\n\n然後，一個大人朝他走過來。嘴巴一張一合。\n\n三個字。\n\n「……」林澈閉上眼睛。\n\n那三個字，還是聽不見。\n\n可是這一次，他沒有頭痛。\n\n他站起來，拍拍膝蓋上的土。\n\n「明天。」他對著空空的操場說，「明天，我一定會想起來。」\n\n海風把這句話，吹向舊禮堂的方向。\n\n牆上的裂紋，像在回應他一樣，閃了一下。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 11 — The Genius and Her Best Friends\n\n2:10 in the afternoon. The investigation headquarters was set up in the World B classroom.\n\nThe two-class investigation team split into three groups: Ching-Ching and B Ching-Ching handled interviews; Xiao-Yang and A-Da hunted for clues around the campus; and Hsiao-Yun... all by herself, handled putting every clue together.\n\nThe blackboard was covered in sticky notes. Each one was a \"difference between the two worlds.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun stood before the blackboard, her eyes behind her glasses frighteningly focused.\n\nShe did one thing: she rearranged the sticky notes by \"time.\"\n\n\"Everyone, help me remember,\" she said. \"When was the earliest time you felt 'this world is strange'?\"\n\nThe interviews began, one by one.\n\nB A-Bao: \"I remember not long after school started, Lin Che suddenly got super popular. Everyone said he could run really fast.\"\n\nA Hsiao-Mei: \"Our Lin Che? He's always been really quiet.\"\n\nB Student: \"The PE class on the third day of school — the whole class went crazy! Lin Che ran the anchor leg and won!\"\n\nA Student: \"PE class? The third day? Wasn't that just picking runners? Nothing special.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun paced back and forth before the blackboard, writing down every sentence she heard on sticky notes.\n\n\"The earliest 'differences' you all remember land on the exact same time.\" She pushed up her glasses.\n\n\"The first week of school. And specifically — PE class.\"\n\n\"Wait.\" Ching-Ching stood up. \"You mean before that, the two worlds were completely identical?\"\n\n\"Yes.\" Hsiao-Yun nodded. \"If the two worlds branched apart at some moment, then everyone's memories before that moment should be exactly the same.\"\n\n\"We just have to find the 'first memory that differs,' and we'll find the branching point.\"\n\nXiao-Yang clapped: \"A genius is a genius!\"\n\nB Hsiao-Yun's friends cheered from the side too: \"Go Hsiao-Yun!\" \"Hsiao-Yun is our brain!\"\n\nA ponytail girl ran out of the classroom and came back carrying two bottles of juice.\n\n\"Here!\" She stuffed one into B Hsiao-Yun's hands and the other into A Hsiao-Yun's. \"You're Hsiao-Yun too, so you get one as well!\"\n\nA Hsiao-Yun took the juice and froze for a few seconds.\n\n\"...Thank you,\" she said quietly, her ears turning red.\n\nLeaning against the door, Lin Che watched this scene, his heart feeling warm.\n\nSuddenly, he heard Hsiao-Yun call his name.\n\n\"Lin Che.\" Hsiao-Yun walked over and stared at him. \"That PE class day — do you remember what you did?\"\n\nLin Che's heart skipped a beat.\n\n\"I... don't remember.\"\n\n\"Not at all?\" Hsiao-Yun's eyes were like two small mirrors.\n\nLin Che shook his head.\n\n\"But the you in World B,\" Hsiao-Yun flipped through her interview notes, \"remembers it perfectly clearly. He remembers taking the anchor leg, winning, being tossed into the air.\"\n\n\"All twenty-six people's memories line up. Only you—\" She looked at him. \"Only your memory is broken.\"\n\nThe classroom went quiet.\n\nLin Che suddenly felt everyone's gaze land on him.\n\n\"So,\" Hsiao-Yun's voice was soft, but it hammered into his ears, \"the branching point isn't just on that day — it's also... connected to you.\"\n\nLin Che opened his mouth, but nothing came out.\n\nInstinctively, he touched his head. The fog seemed to have thinned a little more.\n\nThe playground. The whistle. The warmth of the sun.\n\nThen, blank.\n\n\"It's okay.\" B Lin Che suddenly walked over and patted his shoulder — but stopped halfway, changing it to a \"you can do it\" fist in the air.\n\n\"We'll remember it together,\" he said. \"Two of me added together have to be stronger than one, right?\"\n\nLin Che looked at him and slowly nodded.\n\nThe investigation target was set.\n\nChing-Ching wrote on the blackboard: \"Target: PE class, the third day of school.\"\n\nHsiao-Yun added below it: \"The first memory that differs.\"\n\nEveryone looked at the blackboard, and suddenly felt one step closer to the answer.\n\nJust then, someone at the back of the classroom gasped.\n\n\"The bulletin board!\"\n\nEveryone turned.\n\nOn the bulletin board, An-An's drawings were \"changing channels\" one by one. One second it was a watercolor landscape; the next, it became... an ordinary notice.\n\nLike someone flipping channels with a remote control, frame by frame.\n\nA few seconds later, the bulletin board returned to normal. All the drawings were there, not one missing.\n\n\"The overwriting... has even entered the classroom,\" B Ching-Ching's face went pale.\n\nThe children gathered around the bulletin board and stayed quiet for a long time.\n\nFinally, Xiao-Yang spoke. His voice wasn't as loud as usual.\n\n\"We need to move faster.\"\n\nFour o'clock in the afternoon. In front of the mirror.\n\nThe investigation team prepared to return to World A. Today's progress: the branching point was located.\n\nBefore leaving, B Hsiao-Yun slipped a small note to A Hsiao-Yun.\n\nThe note read: \"Tomorrow is the last day. Let's solve the mystery together.\"\n\nBelow it were two little stick figures holding hands — one with a ponytail, one with round glasses.\n\nA Hsiao-Yun folded the note and tucked it into the deepest part of her pocket.\n\nShe glanced back at World B. The group of best friends were waving at her.\n\nShe didn't wave back. She just said to herself, very quietly:\n\n\"I'm... someone with friends now.\"\n\nThen she stepped into the mirror.\n\nBack in World A. The four of them walked out of the auditorium.\n\nLin Che suddenly stopped.\n\n\"You guys go ahead. I want to be alone for a bit.\"\n\nChing-Ching glanced at him and nodded. A-Da patted his back. Hsiao-Yun pushed up her glasses.\n\nThe three of them left. Lin Che was the only one left on campus.\n\nHe walked to the edge of the playground, crouched down, and touched the red running track.\n\nThe sunset dyed the playground orange. The sea breeze blew in waves.\n\n\"The third day of school...\" he murmured.\n\nHe tried hard to remember. The images of that day flickered like shadows in fog.\n\nThe whistle.\n\nThe sun.\n\nA crowd of people with their heads down.\n\nThen, an adult walked toward him. Mouth opening and closing.\n\nThree words.\n\n\"...\" Lin Che closed his eyes.\n\nThe three words were still inaudible.\n\nBut this time, his head didn't hurt.\n\nHe stood up and brushed the dirt off his knees.\n\n\"Tomorrow,\" he said to the empty playground, \"tomorrow, I will definitely remember.\"\n\nThe sea breeze carried those words toward the old auditorium.\n\nThe cracks on the wall flickered, as if answering him.\n"},{"id":4,"rawContent":"# 第 12 章　安安的畫\n\n下午四點二十分。星期天的校園，安靜得像被按下了暫停鍵。\n\n調查隊正要離開學校，經過六年一班教室時，林澈忽然停下。\n\n教室裡，有聲音。\n\n很輕很輕的、鉛筆在紙上滑動的聲音。\n\n四個人湊到窗邊，往裡看。\n\n教室最後一排，一個女生低著頭，專心地畫著什麼。\n\n是安安。\n\n徐安安，六年一班的「美術股長」——其實這個股長，是大家推來做教室佈置的。她很少講話，存在感很低。\n\n「安安？」阿達大喊。\n\n安安嚇了一大跳，手忙腳亂地把畫本塞進抽屜裡。\n\n「你、你們怎麼還在學校？」她的臉紅了。\n\n「我們才要問你咧！」阿達走進教室，「星期天來學校畫畫？你也太認真了吧！」\n\n安安低著頭，不說話。\n\n晴晴走到她桌邊。抽屜沒關好，露出畫本的一角。封面上，是一片海。\n\n「畫得真好。」晴晴說。\n\n安安愣住了。她看著晴晴，好像不敢相信自己的耳朵。\n\n「真的。」林澈也說，「海浪好像會動一樣。」\n\n安安的臉更紅了。她小聲說：「這是我……唯一喜歡做的事。」\n\n「唯一的嗎？」小筠忽然問。\n\n「嗯。」安安點頭，「媽媽說，畫畫沒什麼用。老師也說，功課比較重要。」\n\n她停了一下：「所以，我都在沒人的時候畫。」\n\n教室裡，安靜了一秒。\n\n「安安。」晴晴忽然說，「你想不想看一個地方？在那裡，你的畫，被貼在牆上。」\n\n安安瞪大眼睛。\n\n傍晚四點五十分。五個人穿過鏡子。\n\n安安是最後一個。她的畫本抱在胸前，抱得緊緊的。\n\nB 世界的六年一班教室。安安走到佈告欄前面。\n\n她抬頭，看了很久很久。\n\n佈告欄上，貼滿了畫。榕樹、海浪、橘色的貓、學校的大門。\n\n每一張，都像她畫的。每一張，又都比她畫的更……大聲。\n\n「這是……我畫的嗎？」她的聲音在抖。\n\n「是『你』畫的。」\n\n安安回頭。\n\n教室門口，站著一個跟她長得一模一樣的女生。齊肩的頭髮，袖口沾著水彩顏料。\n\n是 B 世界的安安。\n\n兩個安安面對面。誰都沒說話。\n\n然後，B 安安忽然笑了。她舉起自己的畫本：「要比比看嗎？」\n\n兩個女生，同時打開畫本。\n\n第一頁，都是海。A 安安的海，安靜，像在嘆氣。B 安安的海，洶湧，像在大笑。\n\n「你畫的海，好安靜。」B 安安說。\n\n「你畫的海，好大聲。」A 安安說。\n\n兩個人，同時笑出來。\n\n「我們班的佈告欄，是我的畫廊。」B 安安說，語氣裡滿是驕傲，「陳老師說，畫畫是禮物。每次有同學過生日，我就畫一張送他。」\n\n「這裡每一個人，都喜歡我的畫。」\n\nA 安安安靜地聽著。她的眼睛，慢慢紅了。\n\n「媽媽說，畫畫沒用。老師說，功課比較重要。」她小聲說，「所以我把畫本，放在抽屜最裡面。」\n\nB 安安看著她，忽然說了一句話。\n\n「可是，你還在畫啊。」\n\nA 安安愣住。\n\n「抽屜最深處，」B 安安說，「你還是每天都在畫。你沒有放棄，不是嗎？」\n\n一滴眼淚，從 A 安安的臉頰滑下來。\n\n可是，她在笑。\n\n「嗯。」她點頭，「我沒有放棄。」\n\nB 安安從畫本上撕下一張畫，塞到她手裡。\n\n是一幅兩個女生並肩看海的畫。畫的背面，寫著一句話：\n\n「給另一個我：繼續畫。」\n\n忽然，教室後面傳來騷動。\n\n「佈告欄又變了！」\n\n大家回頭。\n\n佈告欄上，有三張畫……不見了。取而代之的，是三張印著「校務通知」的紙。\n\n沒有閃爍。沒有換頻道。就只是，安安靜靜地，變了。\n\n「不會變回來了。」B 晴晴的聲音很輕，「這次，是真的『覆蓋』。」\n\n教室裡，安靜得能聽見海風的聲音。\n\n傍晚六點。調查隊準備回家。\n\n走到校門口時，達哥忽然大叫：「書店！書店呢？！」\n\n所有人看向校門口。\n\n原本寫著「海聲書店」的藍色招牌，不見了。\n\n取而代之的，是一塊綠色的 7-ELEVEN 招牌。店裡亮著燈，收銀台後面，站著一個陌生的店員。\n\nB 世界的孩子們，全都呆住了。\n\n「老闆娘呢……」B 晴晴喃喃。\n\n「這裡，變成了我們那邊的小七。」阿達小聲說。\n\n沒人說話。大家就這麼站著，看著那塊綠色的招牌。\n\n六點二十分。五個人穿過鏡子，回到 A 世界。\n\n走出校門時，林澈抬起頭。\n\n綠色的小七招牌，不見了。\n\n取而代之的，是一塊藍色的「海聲書店」招牌。木頭的門框，玻璃門上貼著手寫的推薦小卡。\n\n阿達慢慢走過去，推開玻璃門。\n\n一個綁著頭巾的阿姨抬起頭，笑咪咪的：「哎喲，你們怎麼這麼久沒來了？」\n\n阿達愣住。\n\n「阿姨……你認識我們嗎？」\n\n「怎麼不認識？」老闆娘笑著說，「你們不是常常來買貼紙嗎？來，今天也有新的喔。」\n\n她從圍裙口袋掏出一疊貼紙，一人一張。\n\n林澈接過貼紙。是藍色的小鯨魚。\n\n跟他口袋裡那張——B 世界的貼紙，一模一樣。\n\n他從口袋裡拿出那支藍色鉛筆。\n\n貨架上，排著一整排一模一樣的鉛筆。藍色的筆身，印著「海聲書店」四個字。\n\n「阿姨，」林澈問，「這家店，開了多久了？」\n\n「多久？」老闆娘想了想，「二十幾年了吧。怎麼了？」\n\n林澈搖搖頭：「沒有。只是……覺得很好。」\n\n走出書店，五個人站在海風裡。\n\n晴晴翻開筆記本，寫下：\n\n「第七天，傍晚。覆蓋開始定型。不可逆。」\n\n她抬起頭，看向操場後面的空地。\n\n夕陽下，那圈溜滑梯的影子，已經濃得不像影子了。\n\n幾乎，可以摸到輪廓。\n\n「明天之前……」阿達的聲音很乾，「還會有多少地方，永遠變成另一個世界的樣子？」\n\n沒人回答。\n\n林澈低頭看著手裡的鯨魚貼紙。\n\n兩張貼紙，兩個世界。一模一樣。\n\n他忽然分不清，哪一張，是從哪裡來的。\n\n海風吹過來。書店的招牌，在風裡輕輕晃動。\n\n世界，正在交織。\n\n而第七天，只剩下最後一個夜晚。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 12 — An-An's Drawings\n\n4:20 in the afternoon. The Sunday campus was as quiet as if someone had pressed pause.\n\nThe investigation team was about to leave the school. Passing the Class 6-1 classroom, Lin Che suddenly stopped.\n\nInside the classroom, there was a sound.\n\nA very, very soft sound — the sound of a pencil sliding across paper.\n\nThe four of them moved to the window and peered inside.\n\nIn the last row of the classroom, a girl sat with her head down, drawing something intently.\n\nIt was An-An.\n\nHsu An-An, Class 6-1's \"art officer\" — though really, she'd been voted into the role to handle classroom decorations. She rarely spoke and barely stood out.\n\n\"An-An?\" A-Da shouted.\n\nAn-An jumped, frantically shoving her sketchbook into her desk drawer.\n\n\"Wh-why are you guys still at school?\" Her face turned red.\n\n\"We should be asking you!\" A-Da walked into the classroom. \"Coming to school on a Sunday to draw? You're way too serious!\"\n\nAn-An lowered her head and said nothing.\n\nChing-Ching walked over to her desk. The drawer hadn't closed all the way, and a corner of the sketchbook peeked out. On the cover was a sea.\n\n\"You draw really well,\" Ching-Ching said.\n\nAn-An froze. She looked at Ching-Ching as if she couldn't believe her ears.\n\n\"Really,\" Lin Che added. \"The waves look like they're moving.\"\n\nAn-An's face turned even redder. She said quietly: \"It's... the only thing I like doing.\"\n\n\"The only thing?\" Hsiao-Yun suddenly asked.\n\n\"Mm.\" An-An nodded. \"Mom says drawing is useless. The teacher says schoolwork is more important.\"\n\nShe paused: \"So I only draw when no one is around.\"\n\nThe classroom went quiet for a second.\n\n\"An-An.\" Ching-Ching suddenly said. \"Do you want to see a place where your drawings are hanging on the wall?\"\n\nAn-An's eyes went wide.\n\n4:50 in the evening. The five of them passed through the mirror.\n\nAn-An was the last one. She clutched her sketchbook to her chest, holding it tight.\n\nThe World B Class 6-1 classroom. An-An walked up to the bulletin board.\n\nShe looked up, for a long, long time.\n\nThe bulletin board was covered in drawings. The banyan tree, the ocean waves, the orange cat, the school gate.\n\nEach one looked like something she would draw. And each one was... louder than anything she'd ever drawn.\n\n\"Is this... drawn by me?\" Her voice trembled.\n\n\"By 'you,' yes.\"\n\nAn-An turned around.\n\nAt the classroom door stood a girl who looked exactly like her. Shoulder-length hair, watercolor stains on her cuffs.\n\nIt was the An-An of World B.\n\nThe two An-Ans stood face to face. Neither said a word.\n\nThen B An-An suddenly smiled. She raised her own sketchbook: \"Want to compare?\"\n\nThe two girls opened their sketchbooks at the same time.\n\nThe first page of both was a sea. A An-An's sea was quiet, like a sigh. B An-An's sea was surging, like laughter.\n\n\"Your sea is so quiet,\" B An-An said.\n\n\"Your sea is so loud,\" A An-An said.\n\nThe two of them burst out laughing at the same time.\n\n\"Our class bulletin board is my gallery,\" B An-An said, her voice full of pride. \"Teacher Chen says drawing is a gift. Every time a classmate has a birthday, I draw a picture for them.\"\n\n\"Everyone here loves my drawings.\"\n\nA An-An listened quietly. Her eyes slowly reddened.\n\n\"Mom says drawing is useless. The teacher says schoolwork matters more.\" She said softly. \"So I keep my sketchbook in the deepest part of my drawer.\"\n\nB An-An looked at her and suddenly said one thing.\n\n\"But you're still drawing.\"\n\nA An-An froze.\n\n\"In the deepest part of your drawer,\" B An-An said, \"you still draw every single day. You haven't given up, have you?\"\n\nA tear slid down A An-An's cheek.\n\nBut she was smiling.\n\n\"Mm.\" She nodded. \"I haven't given up.\"\n\nB An-An tore a drawing from her sketchbook and pressed it into her hands.\n\nIt was a picture of two girls watching the sea side by side. On the back was written:\n\n\"To the other me: keep drawing.\"\n\nSuddenly, a commotion came from the back of the classroom.\n\n\"The bulletin board changed again!\"\n\nEveryone turned.\n\nOn the bulletin board, three drawings... were gone. In their place were three sheets printed with \"School Office Notice.\"\n\nNo flickering. No channel-changing. It had simply, silently, changed.\n\n\"It won't change back.\" B Ching-Ching's voice was soft. \"This time, it's real overwriting.\"\n\nThe classroom fell so quiet you could hear the sea breeze.\n\nSix o'clock in the evening. The investigation team got ready to go home.\n\nAs they reached the school gate, Da-ge suddenly yelled: \"The bookstore! Where's the bookstore?!\"\n\nEveryone looked toward the gate.\n\nThe blue sign that read \"Haisheng Bookstore\" was gone.\n\nIn its place hung a green 7-ELEVEN sign. The store was lit, and behind the counter stood a stranger in a store uniform.\n\nThe World B children all stood frozen.\n\n\"The boss lady...\" B Ching-Ching murmured.\n\n\"This place has become the 7-Eleven from our side,\" A-Da said quietly.\n\nNo one spoke. They just stood there, staring at the green sign.\n\n6:20 p.m. The five passed through the mirror and returned to World A.\n\nAs they walked out of the school gate, Lin Che looked up.\n\nThe green 7-ELEVEN sign was gone.\n\nIn its place hung a blue \"Haisheng Bookstore\" sign. A wooden door frame, with a handwritten recommendation card taped to the glass door.\n\nA-Da walked over slowly and pushed the glass door open.\n\nAn auntie with a kerchief on her head looked up, beaming: \"Oh my, why haven't you kids come by in so long?\"\n\nA-Da froze.\n\n\"Auntie... you know us?\"\n\n\"How could I not know you?\" the boss lady laughed. \"Aren't you the ones who always come in for stickers? Here, there are new ones today too.\"\n\nShe pulled a stack of stickers from her apron pocket, one for each of them.\n\nLin Che took his sticker. A small blue whale.\n\nExactly the same as the one in his pocket — the one from World B.\n\nHe pulled the blue pencil out of his pocket.\n\nOn the shelf sat a whole row of identical pencils. Blue bodies, with the words \"Haisheng Bookstore\" printed on them.\n\n\"Auntie,\" Lin Che asked, \"how long has this store been here?\"\n\n\"How long?\" The boss lady thought for a moment. \"Over twenty years, I'd say. Why?\"\n\nLin Che shook his head: \"No reason. It just... feels nice.\"\n\nOutside the bookstore, the five of them stood in the sea breeze.\n\nChing-Ching opened her notebook and wrote:\n\n\"Day seven, evening. The overwriting has begun to set. Irreversible.\"\n\nShe looked up toward the empty lot behind the playground.\n\nIn the sunset, the shadow of the slide had grown so dense it no longer looked like a shadow.\n\nIts outline could almost be touched.\n\n\"Before tomorrow...\" A-Da's voice was dry. \"How many more places will permanently turn into the other world's version?\"\n\nNo one answered.\n\nLin Che looked down at the whale stickers in his hand.\n\nTwo stickers, two worlds. Identical.\n\nHe suddenly couldn't tell which one had come from where.\n\nThe sea breeze blew over. The bookstore's sign swayed gently in the wind.\n\nThe worlds were weaving together.\n\nAnd the seventh day had only one last night left.\n"},{"id":5,"rawContent":"# 第 13 章　覆蓋來襲\n\n晚上七點。海聲國小的孩子們，都回到了自己家。\n\n可是這一夜，沒有一個人睡得著。\n\n林澈坐在書桌前，盯著課本角落畫的那面小鏡子。\n\n忽然，那面「畫出來的鏡子」，閃了一下。\n\n銀白色的光，一閃即逝。像真的鏡子一樣。\n\n林澈揉了揉眼睛。課本還是課本。可是他的心跳，快得嚇人。\n\n同一時間，晴晴的房間裡。\n\n晴晴正翻開筆記本，複習今天的紀錄。\n\n忽然，她愣住了。\n\n筆記本上的字，變了。\n\n「第六天，鏡子提早開、延後關」——這行字的筆跡，慢慢地、慢慢地，變成了另一種筆跡。\n\n那是 B 晴晴的字。\n\n幾秒鐘後，字又變了回來。\n\n晴晴的手，微微發抖。她把筆記本閤上，又打開。字，已經恢復原狀。\n\n阿達的房間裡。\n\n阿達躺在床上，看著書桌上那顆草莓。檯燈照著它，紅得像顆小太陽。\n\n忽然，他對面的牆上，出現了一排影子。\n\n很多很多的影子，像卡片，像信，像同學們舉起來的手。\n\n一閃，就消失了。\n\n阿達從床上坐起來，盯著那面空白的牆。\n\n小筠的房間裡。\n\n小筠在看 B 小筠給她的紙條。兩個牽手的小人，一個馬尾，一個圓眼鏡。\n\n忽然，她書桌旁邊，出現了一把椅子的影子。\n\n像有人，剛剛坐下來，陪她一起看書。\n\n然後，影子消失了。\n\n小筠伸出手，輕輕碰了碰那個位置。什麼都沒有。\n\n群組訊息，響了。\n\n晴晴：「大家……你們家有沒有發生奇怪的事？」\n\n林澈：「有。」\n\n阿達：「有！！」\n\n小筠：「有。」\n\n安安：「我……我畫本上的畫，剛剛自己動了一下。」\n\n晴晴：「覆蓋，已經不只在學校了。它在每一個角落。」\n\n阿達：「那怎麼辦？」\n\n晴晴：「回學校。我們需要所有人。」\n\n晚上八點。海聲國小的操場上，亮起了一盞一盞的手電筒。\n\n六年一班的二十六個孩子，全都來了。有人騎腳踏車，有人用跑的，還有人穿著拖鞋就衝出來了。\n\n舊禮堂的鏡子，大開著。銀白色的光，把整個禮堂照得像白天。\n\n鏡子的另一邊，B 世界的二十六個孩子，也全都到了。\n\n五十二個人，隔著一面鏡子，在最後一個夜晚集合。\n\n「我們都看到了。」B 晴晴說，「我們這裡的屋子、街道，也都在變。」\n\n「所以，」小陽的聲音沒有了平常的大笑，卻很穩，「今天晚上，我們五十二個人一起把謎解開。誰都不許放棄。」\n\n「誰都不許放棄！」孩子們一起喊。\n\n阿寶忽然走到 B 阿寶面前。\n\n「對不起。」他說，「星期六那天，是我們先說你們是假貨的。」\n\nB 阿寶愣了一下，抓抓頭：「我也有錯啦。是我先笑你們沒有書店的。」\n\n兩個人對看一眼，忽然同時笑了。\n\n「扯平了。」\n\n操場上，孩子們分成三組。\n\n第一組，晴晴和 B 晴晴帶隊：把兩個世界所有「被覆蓋」的地方，畫成地圖。\n\n第二組，小筠和 B 小筠帶隊：把所有訪談紀錄，按時間排成一條線。\n\n第三組，小陽和阿達帶隊：檢查校園每個角落，看還有哪裡在變。\n\n而林澈，被 B 林澈拉到操場邊的紅跑道上。\n\n「來。」B 林澈說，「你坐在這裡。」\n\n林澈坐在跑道邊。夜裡的操場，被路燈照得半明半暗。\n\nB 林澈站在他面前，深吸一口氣。\n\n「我把那天，從頭到尾，講給你聽。」\n\n「開學第三天，體育課。劉老師吹哨子，叫大家集合，選大隊接力的人。」\n\n林澈的心跳，開始加速。\n\n「全班都低頭，沒人敢接最後一棒。包括我。我站在隊伍的最後面，頭低低的。」\n\n「然後，劉老師看到了我。」\n\n林澈的手，不自覺地抓緊了跑道。\n\n「他走到我面前，跟我說——」\n\nB 林澈的聲音，像從很遠的地方傳來：\n\n「你想試試看嗎？我看你可以。」\n\n林澈的頭，忽然劇烈地痛起來。\n\n霧。好濃的霧。他拼命想撥開，可是霧裡，什麼都看不見。\n\n「然後呢……」他的聲音在抖。\n\n「然後，我接下了最後一棒。」B 林澈說，「我跑。風好大。全班在叫我的名字。」\n\n林澈閉上眼睛。那些畫面，好像一閃一閃地，在霧的後面浮現。\n\n紅色的跑道。白色的終點線。一雙雙揮舞的手。\n\n可是，那是 B 林澈的畫面。不是他的。\n\n他睜開眼睛，搖了搖。\n\n「還是不行……」他的聲音很沮喪，「我還是想不起來，我的那天。」\n\nB 林澈看著他，忽然蹲下來，與他平視。\n\n「你知道嗎？」B 林澈說，「我們兩個的記憶，隔著一面鏡子。」\n\n「你的記憶缺了一塊，我的記憶卻多了一塊。如果我們一起——」\n\n他舉起手，攤開手掌。\n\n「今晚，在分岔點發生的地方，我們再握一次手。」\n\n林澈看著那隻手。\n\n上一次握手，他看見了 B 林澈的勝利。\n\n如果今晚，在這個地方，在跑道邊——\n\n說不定，霧就會散開。\n\n「好。」林澈說。\n\n他伸出手——\n\n就在兩隻手快要碰到的瞬間，禮堂的方向，忽然爆出一道強光。\n\n「鏡子！」有人尖叫。\n\n所有人看向舊禮堂。\n\n鏡子的光，比白天還亮。銀白色的光芒沖天而起，在操場上空，投出了一個畫面。\n\n畫面裡，是一個巨大的時鐘。\n\n時鐘的指針，正指向……十一點。\n\n然後，時鐘走動起來。滴答。滴答。\n\n指針走過十一點五十九分。\n\n下一秒，畫面裡的世界——整個世界——像沙子一樣，慢慢地、慢慢地散掉了。\n\n五十二個孩子，仰著頭，看著那個畫面，誰都說不出話來。\n\n時鐘消失了。鏡子的光，恢復成原來的銀白色。\n\n「那是……」阿達的聲音抖得不成樣子，「那是什麼意思？」\n\n「第七天結束。」晴晴的聲音，從沒有像現在這樣嚴肅，「如果第七天結束前，我們沒有把謎解開——」\n\n「其中一個世界，會像那樣消失。」\n\n操場上，安靜得可怕。\n\n海風吹過來。路燈下的孩子們，影子拉得好長好長。\n\n小陽低頭看手錶。\n\n「現在，是晚上九點。」\n\n「離午夜，還有三個小時。」\n\n五十二個人，同時看向舊禮堂那面鏡子。\n\n最後一夜，開始了。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 13 — The Overwriting Strikes\n\nSeven o'clock in the evening. The children of Haisheng Elementary had all gone back to their homes.\n\nBut on this night, not one of them could sleep.\n\nLin Che sat at his desk, staring at the little mirror he'd drawn in the corner of his textbook.\n\nSuddenly, that \"drawn mirror\" flickered.\n\nSilvery-white light, flashing once and gone. Like a real mirror.\n\nLin Che rubbed his eyes. The textbook was still just a textbook. But his heart was pounding frighteningly fast.\n\nAt the same time, in Ching-Ching's room.\n\nChing-Ching was flipping open her notebook, reviewing today's records.\n\nSuddenly, she froze.\n\nThe writing in her notebook had changed.\n\n\"Day six, the mirror opened early and closed late\" — the handwriting of that line slowly, slowly turned into another handwriting.\n\nIt was B Ching-Ching's handwriting.\n\nA few seconds later, the writing changed back.\n\nChing-Ching's hand trembled slightly. She closed the notebook, then opened it again. The writing had already returned to normal.\n\nIn A-Da's room.\n\nA-Da lay in bed, looking at the strawberry on his desk. Under the desk lamp, it glowed red like a tiny sun.\n\nSuddenly, on the wall across from him, a row of shadows appeared.\n\nMany, many shadows — like cards, like letters, like classmates' raised hands.\n\nOne flash, and they were gone.\n\nA-Da sat up in bed, staring at the blank wall.\n\nIn Hsiao-Yun's room.\n\nHsiao-Yun was looking at the note B Hsiao-Yun had given her. Two little stick figures holding hands — one with a ponytail, one with round glasses.\n\nSuddenly, beside her desk, the shadow of a chair appeared.\n\nAs if someone had just sat down to keep her company while she read.\n\nThen, the shadow vanished.\n\nHsiao-Yun reached out and gently touched that spot. Nothing.\n\nThe group chat buzzed.\n\nChing-Ching: \"Everyone... did anything strange happen at your homes?\"\n\nLin Che: \"Yes.\"\n\nA-Da: \"Yes!!\"\n\nHsiao-Yun: \"Yes.\"\n\nAn-An: \"I... the drawings in my sketchbook just moved on their own.\"\n\nChing-Ching: \"The overwriting isn't just at school anymore. It's in every corner.\"\n\nA-Da: \"Then what do we do?\"\n\nChing-Ching: \"Come back to school. We need everyone.\"\n\nEight o'clock at night. On the Haisheng Elementary playground, flashlight after flashlight flicked on.\n\nAll twenty-six children of Class 6-1 had come. Some by bike, some running, some dashing out in slippers.\n\nThe mirror in the old auditorium was wide open. Its silvery-white light made the auditorium bright as day.\n\nOn the other side of the mirror, the twenty-six children of World B had all arrived too.\n\nFifty-two people, gathered on the final night, across a single mirror.\n\n\"We've all seen it,\" B Ching-Ching said. \"Our houses and streets here are changing too.\"\n\n\"So,\" Xiao-Yang's voice had lost its usual booming laugh, but it was steady, \"tonight, all fifty-two of us will solve this mystery together. No one is allowed to give up.\"\n\n\"No one gives up!\" the children shouted together.\n\nA-Bao suddenly walked up to B A-Bao.\n\n\"I'm sorry,\" he said. \"On Saturday, we were the ones who called you fakes first.\"\n\nB A-Bao blinked and scratched his head: \"I was wrong too. I'm the one who laughed at you for not having a bookstore.\"\n\nThe two of them glanced at each other, then suddenly laughed at the same time.\n\n\"Even.\"\n\nOn the playground, the children split into three groups.\n\nGroup One, led by Ching-Ching and B Ching-Ching: map out every \"overwritten\" place in both worlds.\n\nGroup Two, led by Hsiao-Yun and B Hsiao-Yun: line up all the interview records by time.\n\nGroup Three, led by Xiao-Yang and A-Da: check every corner of the campus to see where else things were changing.\n\nAs for Lin Che, B Lin Che pulled him over to the red running track at the edge of the playground.\n\n\"Come,\" B Lin Che said. \"Sit here.\"\n\nLin Che sat at the edge of the track. At night, the playground was half-lit by the street lamps.\n\nB Lin Che stood before him and took a deep breath.\n\n\"I'll tell you that day, from beginning to end.\"\n\n\"The third day of school, PE class. Coach Liu blew his whistle and called everyone together to pick the relay team.\"\n\nLin Che's heartbeat began to speed up.\n\n\"The whole class looked down. Nobody dared take the anchor leg. Including me. I stood at the very back of the line, head bowed.\"\n\n\"Then, Coach Liu saw me.\"\n\nLin Che's hand unconsciously gripped the track.\n\n\"He walked up to me and said—\"\n\nB Lin Che's voice came as if from far away:\n\n\"Don't you want to give it a try? I think you can do it.\"\n\nLin Che's head suddenly began to ache fiercely.\n\nFog. Such thick fog. He tried desperately to push it aside, but inside the fog, nothing was visible.\n\n\"Then what...\" his voice trembled.\n\n\"Then I took the anchor leg,\" B Lin Che said. \"I ran. The wind was so strong. The whole class was shouting my name.\"\n\nLin Che closed his eyes. Those images seemed to flicker, rising up behind the fog.\n\nThe red track. The white finish line. A sea of waving hands.\n\nBut those were B Lin Che's images. Not his.\n\nHe opened his eyes and shook his head.\n\n\"Still no good...\" his voice was full of frustration. \"I still can't remember my version of that day.\"\n\nB Lin Che looked at him, then suddenly crouched down to meet his eyes.\n\n\"You know what?\" B Lin Che said. \"Our two memories are separated by a mirror.\"\n\n\"Your memory has a missing piece, and mine has an extra piece. If we put them together—\"\n\nHe raised his hand and opened his palm.\n\n\"Tonight, at the place where the branching happened, let's hold hands once more.\"\n\nLin Che looked at that hand.\n\nThe last time they held hands, he'd seen B Lin Che's victory.\n\nIf tonight, in this place, at the edge of the track—\n\nMaybe the fog would clear.\n\n\"Okay,\" Lin Che said.\n\nHe reached out his hand—\n\nJust as the two hands were about to touch, a blinding light erupted from the direction of the auditorium.\n\n\"The mirror!\" someone screamed.\n\nEveryone looked toward the old auditorium.\n\nThe mirror's light was brighter than daylight. The silvery-white glow shot into the sky, and above the playground, it projected an image.\n\nIn the image was a giant clock.\n\nThe clock's hands were pointing at... eleven.\n\nThen the clock began to move. Tick. Tock.\n\nThe hands swept past 11:59.\n\nThe next second, the world in the image — the entire world — crumbled away like sand, slowly, slowly.\n\nThe fifty-two children tilted their heads up, staring at that image. None of them could say a word.\n\nThe clock vanished. The mirror's light returned to its original silvery-white.\n\n\"What...\" A-Da's voice shook uncontrollably. \"What does that mean?\"\n\n\"The end of the seventh day,\" Ching-Ching said, her voice more serious than it had ever been. \"If we haven't solved the mystery before the seventh day ends—\"\n\n\"One of the worlds will vanish, just like that.\"\n\nThe playground fell terrifyingly silent.\n\nThe sea breeze blew over. Under the street lamps, the children's shadows stretched long, long.\n\nXiao-Yang looked down at his watch.\n\n\"Right now, it's nine o'clock at night.\"\n\n\"Three hours until midnight.\"\n\nThe fifty-two people turned toward the mirror in the old auditorium at the same time.\n\nThe final night had begun.\n"},{"id":6,"rawContent":"# 第 14 章　體育課的那句話\n\n晚上九點十分。操場上，五十二個孩子沒有散。\n\n時鐘的畫面消失了。可是那個畫面，會一直留在大家心裡。\n\n「還有三個小時。」小陽說。他看著所有人，「可是我們不只有三個小時。我們有五十二個人。」\n\n孩子們互相看了看。不知道是誰先開始的，慢慢地，大家都用力點了一下頭。\n\nB 林澈走到林澈面前。\n\n「準備好了嗎？」\n\n林澈看著他。喉嚨很乾。他想起剛才的霧，想起那些聽不見的字。\n\n「準備好了。」他說。\n\n兩個人走到跑道的轉彎處。\n\n「這裡。」B 林澈說，「劉老師那時候，就站在這裡。而你，站在這裡。」\n\n他往後退了兩步，指了指腳下的地面。\n\n林澈低頭。跑道上的白色起跑線，在月光下微微發亮。\n\n兩個人面對面站好。\n\n「可能會很痛。」B 林澈說，「想起遺忘的事，有時候，像把傷口上的疤撕開。」\n\n「沒關係。」林澈說，「我已經……痛很久了。」\n\nB 林澈看著他，伸出手。\n\n林澈伸出手。\n\n兩隻手，在月光下，握在一起。\n\n銀白色的光，從指縫間溢出。\n\n記憶，像打開的水壩，洶湧而來。\n\n林澈看見了。\n\n九月。陽光。操場。\n\n劉老師的哨子聲，尖銳地劃過天空。\n\n「今天，我們要選大隊接力的選手。」劉老師的聲音，洪亮又溫暖，「最後一棒，誰想試試？」\n\n全班二十六個人，低著頭。你看我，我看你，沒有一個人舉手。\n\n林澈站在隊伍的最後面。他的手，慢慢地、慢慢地，舉起來一點點。\n\n只有一點點。像一隻剛學飛的鳥，猶豫著，要不要離開樹枝。\n\n劉老師的眼睛，掃過全班。\n\n他看到林澈了。\n\n他走過來。一步，兩步，三步。\n\n林澈的心跳得很快。他的半隻手，還舉在半空中。\n\n「你比較文靜。」劉老師笑了笑，語氣很溫和，「最後一棒這種事，還是讓給跑得快的同學吧。」\n\n那隻舉到一半的手，垂了下去。\n\n像一隻鳥，收了翅膀，回到樹枝上。從此，再也沒有飛起來過。\n\n「……」林澈看著那個自己。\n\n他看到自己低下頭，退到隊伍最後面，退到窗邊，退到角落。\n\n他看到自己，再也沒有舉過手。上課不舉手，下課不說話，連別人叫他的名字，都要慢半拍才回頭。\n\n然後，畫面像快轉的電影。\n\n他看到阿達在講台上講笑話。全班笑完就散，沒有人聽他接下來要說的活動。\n\n他看到小筠一個人坐在最後一排，低著頭吃便當。\n\n他看到安安把畫本，塞進抽屜的最深處。\n\n他看到空空的操場後方——那個本來應該有一座溜滑梯的地方。\n\n這些畫面，一幕一幕地閃過。\n\n然後，霧，散了。\n\n「哈啊——」\n\n林澈跪倒在跑道上，大口喘氣。\n\n眼淚，一顆一顆，掉在紅色的跑道上。\n\n「我想起來了……」他的聲音沙啞，「我全都想起來了。」\n\n「他說，我比較文靜。」\n\n「他說，讓給跑得快的同學。」\n\n操場上，安靜得只剩下他的呼吸聲。\n\n五十二個孩子，靜靜地圍了過來。\n\n「就是那句話。」晴晴的聲音很輕，「分歧點，就是那句話。」\n\n「我們這邊，劉老師說的是『我看你可以』。」B 林澈說，「你們那邊，劉老師說的是『讓給跑得快的』。」\n\n「同一天，同一個地方，同一個人。」小陽接話，「可是說出口的話，不一樣。」\n\n「所以，兩個世界，從那一句話開始，分開了。」小筠說。\n\n孩子們你看我，我看你。這個謎底，又簡單，又沉重。\n\n「劉老師……」林澈低聲說，「他是故意的嗎？他是覺得，我不行嗎？」\n\n「他不是故意的。」B 林澈走到他旁邊，蹲下來，「他只是，在那個世界，看到了那個你。」\n\n「他怕你受傷。他其實，是在保護你。」\n\n林澈抬起頭。\n\n「在我們這邊，劉老師看到的是『想試試看的我』。所以，他推了我一把。」B 林澈說，「在你們那邊，他看到的可能是『很緊張的我』。所以，他拉了我一把。」\n\n「兩句話，都是為你好。只是，結果完全不一樣。」\n\n林澈低下頭，眼淚又掉了下來。\n\n可是這一次，他覺得心裡有什麼東西，鬆開了。\n\n「我知道了。」他說，「那句話，不是我的錯。也不是劉老師的錯。」\n\n「它只是……其中一種可能。」\n\n晴晴翻開筆記本，寫下最後一行：\n\n「分歧點確認：開學第三天，體育課，劉老師對林澈說的那句話。」\n\n「現在的問題是，」小筠推了推眼鏡，「知道了分歧點，然後呢？」\n\n「要怎麼，把兩個世界『修回去』？」\n\n沒人知道答案。\n\n海風吹過來。路燈下，孩子們的影子搖搖晃晃。\n\n「也許……」林澈忽然開口。他的聲音還是啞啞的，可是很堅定。\n\n「也許，我們應該回到那天。」\n\n所有人看向他。\n\n「回到劉老師開口之前的那一刻。」林澈站起來，看著鏡子的方向，「不是為了改變它。是為了……面對它。」\n\n晴晴的眼睛亮起來。\n\n「重演。」她說，「如果我們在分岔點，把那天重演一遍——鏡子，會不會帶我們回到那一刻？」\n\n「有可能。」小筠說，「鏡子會回應我們。它一直都在回應我們。」\n\n「那還等什麼？」小陽捲起袖子，「比賽啊！」\n\n孩子們忽然都有了幹勁。\n\n五十二個人，往操場中央集合。\n\n就在這時，阿達忽然指著操場後面：「你們看！」\n\n空地上，那圈溜滑梯的影子，在月光下，幾乎變成了一座真的溜滑梯。\n\n阿達撿起一顆小石頭，丟過去。\n\n「鏘。」\n\n石頭撞在影子上，發出了聲音。\n\n就像撞在真正的鐵皮上。\n\n孩子們全都愣住了。\n\n「它快過來了……」阿達的聲音發抖。\n\n「我們也要快。」晴晴說。\n\n她低頭看手錶。\n\n「九點五十分。」\n\n五十二個人，站在月光下的操場上。\n\n牆上的裂紋，像銀色的藤蔓，從禮堂一路爬向操場。\n\n而在他們頭頂，那座巨大的時鐘，正無聲地，走向午夜。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 14 — The Words from PE Class\n\n9:10 at night. On the playground, the fifty-two children had not dispersed.\n\nThe clock's image had vanished. But that image would stay in everyone's hearts.\n\n\"Three hours left,\" Xiao-Yang said. He looked at everyone. \"But we don't just have three hours. We have fifty-two people.\"\n\nThe children glanced at one another. No one knew who started it, but slowly, everyone gave a firm nod.\n\nB Lin Che walked up to Lin Che.\n\n\"Ready?\"\n\nLin Che looked at him. His throat was dry. He thought of the fog from earlier, and the words he couldn't hear.\n\n\"Ready,\" he said.\n\nThe two of them walked to the bend in the track.\n\n\"Here,\" B Lin Che said. \"That day, Coach Liu stood right here. And you stood here.\"\n\nHe stepped back two paces and pointed at the ground beneath his feet.\n\nLin Che looked down. The white starting line on the track glowed faintly in the moonlight.\n\nThe two of them stood facing each other.\n\n\"It might hurt,\" B Lin Che said. \"Remembering forgotten things is sometimes like tearing the scar off a wound.\"\n\n\"It's fine,\" Lin Che said. \"I've... been hurting for a long time already.\"\n\nB Lin Che looked at him and held out his hand.\n\nLin Che held out his hand.\n\nThe two hands clasped together under the moonlight.\n\nSilvery-white light spilled from between their fingers.\n\nMemories came surging in, like a dam bursting open.\n\nLin Che saw it.\n\nSeptember. Sunshine. The playground.\n\nCoach Liu's whistle sliced sharply through the sky.\n\n\"Today, we're picking our relay team.\" Coach Liu's voice was loud and warm. \"The anchor leg — who wants to try?\"\n\nAll twenty-six students had their heads down. You looked at me, I looked at you — not one hand went up.\n\nLin Che stood at the very back of the line. His hand slowly, slowly rose just a little.\n\nJust a little. Like a baby bird learning to fly, hesitating over whether to leave the branch.\n\nCoach Liu's eyes swept across the class.\n\nHe saw Lin Che.\n\nHe walked over. One step, two steps, three steps.\n\nLin Che's heart pounded. His half-raised hand was still in the air.\n\n\"You're more on the quiet side.\" Coach Liu smiled, his tone gentle. \"For the anchor leg, let's leave it to the kids who run fast.\"\n\nThe half-raised hand dropped.\n\nLike a bird folding its wings and returning to the branch. Never to fly again.\n\n\"...\" Lin Che watched that version of himself.\n\nHe watched himself lower his head, retreat to the back of the line, retreat to the window, retreat to the corner.\n\nHe watched himself never raise his hand again. Never raising his hand in class, never speaking at recess — even when someone called his name, it took him an extra beat to turn around.\n\nThen the images became a fast-forwarding film.\n\nHe saw A-Da telling jokes on the podium. The class laughed and scattered, and no one listened to the activity he was about to propose.\n\nHe saw Hsiao-Yun sitting alone in the last row, eating her lunch box with her head down.\n\nHe saw An-An shoving her sketchbook into the deepest part of her drawer.\n\nHe saw the empty space behind the playground — the place where a slide should have stood.\n\nThese images flashed by, one after another.\n\nThen, the fog lifted.\n\n\"Ahh—\"\n\nLin Che collapsed onto his knees on the track, gasping for air.\n\nTears fell onto the red track, one by one.\n\n\"I remember now...\" his voice was hoarse. \"I remember everything.\"\n\n\"He said I was quiet.\"\n\n\"He said, leave it to the kids who run fast.\"\n\nThe playground went so silent that only his breathing remained.\n\nThe fifty-two children quietly gathered around.\n\n\"It was that sentence.\" Ching-Ching's voice was soft. \"The branching point was that sentence.\"\n\n\"On our side, Coach Liu said, 'I think you can do it,'\" B Lin Che said. \"On your side, Coach Liu said, 'Leave it to the kids who run fast.'\"\n\n\"The same day, the same place, the same person,\" Xiao-Yang picked up. \"But the words that came out were different.\"\n\n\"So the two worlds split apart from that one sentence,\" Hsiao-Yun said.\n\nThe children looked at one another. The answer was so simple, and so heavy.\n\n\"Coach Liu...\" Lin Che said quietly. \"Did he do it on purpose? Did he think I couldn't do it?\"\n\n\"He didn't do it on purpose.\" B Lin Che walked over and crouched beside him. \"In that world, he just saw that version of you.\"\n\n\"He was afraid you'd get hurt. He was actually protecting you.\"\n\nLin Che looked up.\n\n\"On our side, Coach Liu saw a 'me who wanted to try.' So he gave me a push,\" B Lin Che said. \"On your side, he probably saw a 'very nervous me.' So he pulled me back.\"\n\n\"Both sentences were meant to be kind. It's just that the results were completely different.\"\n\nLin Che lowered his head, and the tears fell again.\n\nBut this time, he felt something inside him loosen.\n\n\"I understand now,\" he said. \"That sentence wasn't my fault. And it wasn't Coach Liu's fault.\"\n\n\"It was just... one of the possibilities.\"\n\nChing-Ching opened her notebook and wrote the final line:\n\n\"Branching point confirmed: PE class, the third day of school. The sentence Coach Liu said to Lin Che.\"\n\n\"Now the question is,\" Hsiao-Yun pushed up her glasses, \"now that we know the branching point, what next?\"\n\n\"How do we 'fix' the two worlds back?\"\n\nNo one knew the answer.\n\nThe sea breeze blew over. Under the street lamps, the children's shadows swayed.\n\n\"Maybe...\" Lin Che suddenly spoke. His voice was still hoarse, but firm.\n\n\"Maybe we should go back to that day.\"\n\nEveryone looked at him.\n\n\"Back to the moment before Coach Liu opened his mouth.\" Lin Che stood up and looked toward the mirror. \"Not to change it. But to... face it.\"\n\nChing-Ching's eyes lit up.\n\n\"A re-enactment,\" she said. \"If we re-stage that day at the branching point — will the mirror take us back to that moment?\"\n\n\"It's possible,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"The mirror responds to us. It's always been responding to us.\"\n\n\"Then what are we waiting for?\" Xiao-Yang rolled up his sleeves. \"Let's race!\"\n\nSuddenly, all the children were filled with energy.\n\nThe fifty-two of them gathered toward the center of the playground.\n\nJust then, A-Da suddenly pointed behind the playground: \"Look!\"\n\nOn the empty lot, the shadow of the slide had almost become a real slide in the moonlight.\n\nA-Da picked up a pebble and threw it.\n\n\"Clang.\"\n\nThe stone struck the shadow and made a sound.\n\nAs if it had hit real sheet metal.\n\nAll the children froze.\n\n\"It's almost here...\" A-Da's voice trembled.\n\n\"We have to hurry too,\" Ching-Ching said.\n\nShe looked down at her watch.\n\n\"9:50.\"\n\nThe fifty-two children stood on the moonlit playground.\n\nThe cracks on the wall, like silver vines, were crawling from the auditorium toward the playground.\n\nAnd above their heads, the giant clock was silently marching toward midnight.\n"},{"id":7,"rawContent":"# 第 15 章　兩個世界的比賽\n\n晚上十點。操場上，五十二個孩子開始「重演那一天」。\n\n阿達自告奮勇當主持人。他爬上司令台，拿手電筒當麥克風。\n\n「現場各位觀眾！歡迎收看——兩個世界的六年一班，世紀大重演！」\n\n孩子們笑成一片。緊張的氣氛，鬆開了一點點。\n\n「肅靜！肅靜！」阿達清清喉嚨，「現在，請劉老師出場！」\n\n小陽從人群中跳出來。他脖子上掛著達哥貢獻的哨子，學劉老師的樣子，把哨子塞進嘴裡。\n\n「嗶——」\n\n哨子聲在夜空下迴盪。孩子們笑得更厲害了。\n\n「不對不對，劉老師才沒有那麼帥。」B 晴晴笑著喊。\n\n「帥不帥不重要，重要的是氣勢！」小陽叉腰。\n\n「集合！六年一班，集合！」他大聲喊。\n\n兩班的每一個人，都跑到了跑道上。\n\n五十二個人，在月光下排成歪歪扭扭的隊伍。\n\n「今天，我們要選大隊接力的選手。」小陽學著劉老師的語氣，居然學得有七分像，「最後一棒，誰想試試？」\n\n孩子們你看我，我看你。然後，很配合地，一起低下了頭。\n\n這一幕，和那天，一模一樣。\n\n林澈站在隊伍最後面。他的手，不知不覺地，舉起來了一點點。\n\n只有一點點。\n\n「你！」小陽的手，指向他。\n\n林澈愣住。\n\n小陽大步走過來，站在他面前，模仿劉老師的聲音：\n\n「你想試試看嗎？我看你可以。」\n\n操場上，安靜了一秒。\n\n然後，不知道是誰先喊的。\n\n「林澈！跑跑看！」\n\n「跑跑看！跑跑看！」五十二個聲音，一起響起來。\n\n林澈看著他們。月光下，一張張臉都亮晶晶的。\n\n他接過阿達遞過來的接力棒——那是一支手電筒。\n\n他站到起跑線上。\n\n「預備——」阿達大喊，「嗶！」\n\n林澈跑了起來。\n\n他已經很久沒有跑得這麼用力了。風從耳邊掠過，夜裡的操場，在他腳下往後飛。\n\n路燈一盞一盞往後退。呼吸越來越重。心跳越來越響。\n\n跑道邊，五十二個孩子追著他跑，一邊跑一邊喊：「林澈！林澈！林澈！」\n\n林澈的眼睛濕了。\n\n終點線，是兩個孩子拉著的一條白手帕。\n\n他衝過去。\n\n「到了！」阿達跳起來，「林澈第一個衝線！」\n\n孩子們一擁而上，把林澈圍在中間。有人拍他的背，有人拉他的手，有人把他舉起來——\n\n「等一下！不能亂碰！」晴晴在旁邊大喊，可是已經來不及了。\n\n林澈被拋上了天空。\n\n他看著夜裡的天空。星星很多，像一顆一顆小燈泡。\n\n那一瞬間，他忽然覺得，心裡那隻收了翅膀的鳥，好像動了一下。\n\n他落到孩子們的手裡。大家笑著，把他放下來。\n\n林澈喘著氣，站在原地。\n\n他笑了。笑著笑著，眼淚又掉了下來。\n\n「喂，你怎麼又哭了！」阿達嚇了一跳。\n\n「不知道。」林澈擦掉眼淚，還是笑，「就覺得……原來被大家看著跑，是這種感覺。」\n\n孩子們安靜了一秒，然後全都笑了。\n\nB 林澈走過來，站在他旁邊。\n\n「很帥吧？」B 林澈說，「被全班叫名字的感覺。」\n\n「很帥。」林澈點頭，「原來，這就是你的世界。」\n\nB 林澈搖搖頭：「這不只是我的世界。」\n\n他指著操場上的每一個人：「這也是你的世界。從今天晚上開始。」\n\n林澈愣住了。\n\n就在這時，舊禮堂的方向，忽然爆出一道銀白色的光。\n\n「鏡子！」孩子們回頭。\n\n鏡子的光沖天而起，比剛才那次更亮。\n\n銀白色的光芒，在操場上空流轉，像一條發光的河。\n\n然後，光慢慢地、慢慢地暗了下去。\n\n恢復成原來的亮度。\n\n「它……回應了。」小筠說，聲音裡有興奮，也有困惑，「可是，它沒有帶我們去任何地方。」\n\n「是不是哪裡不夠？」阿達問。\n\n小筠盯著鏡子，眼鏡反著月光。\n\n「它剛才最亮的時候，是林澈衝線的那一瞬間。」她說，「可是，光還不夠。」\n\n「它想要更多。」小筠轉過頭，「它想要『那天』本身。」\n\n「我們重演的，只是『像那天』。」晴晴接著說，「不是『那天』。」\n\n「那怎麼辦？」小陽皺眉，「我們又不能真的回到過去。」\n\n沒人說話。\n\n林澈低頭，看著手裡的手電筒接力棒。\n\n「也許……」他慢慢地說，「我們必須，把這場重演，帶到鏡子前面。」\n\n所有人看向他。\n\n「那天的事，發生在操場。可是通往那天的路，在鏡子裡。」林澈說。\n\n「如果我們在鏡子前面，把那天再演一次……」\n\n「鏡子，就會打開那扇門。」小筠接話，眼睛亮起來。\n\n孩子們互相看了看。\n\n「那還等什麼？」小陽大喊，「全體移動！」\n\n五十二個人，浩浩蕩蕩地走進舊禮堂。\n\n鏡子前，孩子們圍成一個半圓。\n\n銀白色的光，映在每一張臉上。\n\n鏡子裡，倒映著兩個六年一班。一模一樣的人，一模一樣的緊張，一模一樣的期待。\n\n「來吧。」B 林澈說。\n\n他伸出手。\n\n林澈伸出手。\n\n兩隻手，再一次，握在一起。\n\n沒有痛。沒有霧。\n\n只有很暖、很暖的光。\n\n鏡面，開始泛起漣漪。\n\n就在波紋擴散的瞬間，牆上的裂紋，忽然「喀」地一聲——\n\n往操場的方向，又爬出了一大段。\n\n「快看！」阿達大叫。\n\n裂紋爬過的地方，地面開始變成兩個世界重疊的畫面：一下是草地，一下是水泥地；一下有溜滑梯的影子，一下是空地。\n\n「世界……在加速重疊了。」晴晴的聲音發抖。\n\n她低頭看手錶。\n\n「十點半。」\n\n「離午夜，還有一個半小時。」\n\n鏡子裡，漣漪一圈一圈擴大。\n\n而漣漪的中央，隱隱約約，浮現出了一個畫面——\n\n是陽光。是操場。是一群低著頭的孩子。\n\n是那天。\n\n五十二個人，屏住呼吸。\n\n鏡子，開始「回憶」了。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 15 — The Race Between Two Worlds\n\nTen o'clock at night. On the playground, the fifty-two children began to \"re-stage that day.\"\n\nA-Da volunteered to be the host. He climbed onto the podium and used a flashlight as a microphone.\n\n\"Ladies and gentlemen of the audience! Welcome to — the Class 6-1 of Two Worlds, Century Grand Re-enactment!\"\n\nThe children dissolved into laughter. The tense atmosphere loosened a little.\n\n\"Order! Order!\" A-Da cleared his throat. \"Now, please welcome Coach Liu!\"\n\nXiao-Yang jumped out of the crowd. With the whistle Da-ge had contributed hanging around his neck, he imitated Coach Liu's manner and put the whistle in his mouth.\n\n\"Tweet—\"\n\nThe whistle echoed under the night sky. The children laughed even harder.\n\n\"No, no, Coach Liu isn't that handsome,\" B Ching-Ching called out, laughing.\n\n\"Handsome or not doesn't matter! What matters is the aura!\" Xiao-Yang put his hands on his hips.\n\n\"Line up! Class 6-1, line up!\" he shouted.\n\nEveryone from both classes ran onto the track.\n\nFifty-two people formed a crooked, zigzagging line in the moonlight.\n\n\"Today, we're picking our relay team.\" Xiao-Yang imitated Coach Liu's tone — about seventy percent accurate. \"The anchor leg — who wants to try?\"\n\nThe children looked at one another. Then, playing along perfectly, they all lowered their heads.\n\nThis scene was exactly like that day.\n\nLin Che stood at the back of the line. His hand, without him noticing, rose just a little.\n\nJust a little.\n\n\"You!\" Xiao-Yang's hand pointed at him.\n\nLin Che froze.\n\nXiao-Yang strode over, stood in front of him, and imitated Coach Liu's voice:\n\n\"Don't you want to give it a try? I think you can do it.\"\n\nThe playground went quiet for a second.\n\nThen, no one knew who shouted first.\n\n\"Lin Che! Run!\"\n\n\"Run! Run!\" Fifty-two voices rang out together.\n\nLin Che looked at them. Under the moonlight, every face sparkled.\n\nHe took the baton A-Da handed him — it was a flashlight.\n\nHe stepped up to the starting line.\n\n\"On your marks—\" A-Da yelled. \"Go!\"\n\nLin Che ran.\n\nHe hadn't run this hard in a long time. The wind rushed past his ears. The nighttime playground flew backward beneath his feet.\n\nStreet lamp after street lamp receded. His breathing grew heavier. His heartbeat grew louder.\n\nAlong the track, fifty-two children chased after him, shouting as they ran: \"Lin Che! Lin Che! Lin Che!\"\n\nLin Che's eyes went wet.\n\nThe finish line was a white handkerchief held taut by two kids.\n\nHe charged through it.\n\n\"He made it!\" A-Da jumped up. \"Lin Che is first across the line!\"\n\nThe children swarmed around him. Some patted his back, some grabbed his hands, some lifted him up—\n\n\"Wait! Don't touch him!\" Ching-Ching shouted from the side, but it was already too late.\n\nLin Che was tossed into the sky.\n\nHe looked at the night sky. So many stars, like little light bulbs.\n\nIn that instant, he felt the bird inside him — the one that had folded its wings — stir just a little.\n\nHe landed in the children's hands. Laughing, they set him down.\n\nLin Che stood there, catching his breath.\n\nHe smiled. And as he smiled, tears fell again.\n\n\"Hey, why are you crying again!\" A-Da was startled.\n\n\"I don't know.\" Lin Che wiped his tears, still smiling. \"I just felt... so this is what it's like, running with everyone watching you.\"\n\nThe children went quiet for a second, then all laughed.\n\nB Lin Che walked over and stood beside him.\n\n\"Pretty cool, right?\" B Lin Che said. \"The feeling of the whole class shouting your name.\"\n\n\"Pretty cool.\" Lin Che nodded. \"So this is your world.\"\n\nB Lin Che shook his head: \"This isn't just my world.\"\n\nHe pointed at everyone on the playground: \"This is your world too. Starting tonight.\"\n\nLin Che froze.\n\nJust then, a silvery-white light erupted from the direction of the old auditorium.\n\n\"The mirror!\" The children turned.\n\nThe mirror's light shot into the sky, brighter than the time before.\n\nThe silvery-white glow swirled above the playground, like a glowing river.\n\nThen, the light slowly, slowly dimmed.\n\nIt returned to its original brightness.\n\n\"It... responded,\" Hsiao-Yun said, both excitement and confusion in her voice. \"But it didn't take us anywhere.\"\n\n\"Is something missing?\" A-Da asked.\n\nHsiao-Yun stared at the mirror, her glasses reflecting the moonlight.\n\n\"It was brightest at the moment Lin Che crossed the line,\" she said. \"But the light still wasn't enough.\"\n\n\"It wants more.\" Hsiao-Yun turned around. \"It wants 'that day' itself.\"\n\n\"What we re-staged was only 'like that day,'\" Ching-Ching continued. \"Not 'that day.'\"\n\n\"Then what do we do?\" Xiao-Yang frowned. \"We can't really go back to the past.\"\n\nNo one spoke.\n\nLin Che looked down at the flashlight baton in his hand.\n\n\"Maybe...\" he said slowly, \"we have to bring this re-enactment to the mirror.\"\n\nEveryone looked at him.\n\n\"What happened that day took place on the playground. But the road to that day is inside the mirror,\" Lin Che said.\n\n\"If we act out that day once more, in front of the mirror...\"\n\n\"The mirror will open the door,\" Hsiao-Yun finished, her eyes lighting up.\n\nThe children looked at one another.\n\n\"Then what are we waiting for?\" Xiao-Yang yelled. \"Everyone, move out!\"\n\nThe fifty-two children marched into the old auditorium in a grand procession.\n\nIn front of the mirror, the children formed a semicircle.\n\nThe silvery-white light reflected on every face.\n\nIn the mirror were reflected two Class 6-1s. Identical people, identical nervousness, identical hope.\n\n\"Come on,\" B Lin Che said.\n\nHe held out his hand.\n\nLin Che held out his hand.\n\nThe two hands clasped together once more.\n\nNo pain. No fog.\n\nOnly very, very warm light.\n\nThe mirror's surface began to ripple.\n\nJust as the ripples spread, the cracks on the wall let out a sudden \"crack\"—\n\nAnd crawled another long stretch toward the playground.\n\n\"Look!\" A-Da shouted.\n\nWhere the cracks passed, the ground began showing overlapping images of the two worlds: grass one moment, cement the next; the shadow of a slide one moment, empty land the next.\n\n\"The worlds... are overlapping faster now,\" Ching-Ching's voice trembled.\n\nShe looked down at her watch.\n\n\"10:30.\"\n\n\"An hour and a half until midnight.\"\n\nIn the mirror, the ripples spread wider and wider.\n\nAnd at the center of the ripples, an image faintly emerged—\n\nSunshine. A playground. A crowd of children with their heads down.\n\nThat day.\n\nThe fifty-two children held their breath.\n\nThe mirror had begun to \"remember.\"\n"},{"id":8,"rawContent":"# 第 16 章　鏡裂\n\n鏡子裡的畫面，越來越清楚了。\n\n是白天。是九月。是開學第三天的操場。\n\n陽光亮得刺眼。孩子們甚至能「聞」到畫面裡的味道——草地的味道，海風的味道。\n\n五十二個人擠在鏡子前，沒有一個人說話。\n\n畫面裡，劉老師吹響哨子。\n\n然後，孩子們都看見了。\n\n鏡面，分開了。\n\n鏡子裡的畫面，分成了兩半。\n\n左邊：劉老師走到小小的林澈面前，嘴巴張開——\n\n「你比較文靜。最後一棒，讓給跑得快的同學吧。」\n\n左邊的畫面裡，那個小小的林澈，垂下頭，退了回去。\n\n右邊：劉老師走到小小的林澈面前，嘴巴張開——\n\n「你想試試看嗎？我看你可以。」\n\n右邊的畫面裡，那個小小的林澈，眼睛亮起來，用力點頭。\n\n同樣的一秒。兩種可能。一面鏡子，兩個世界。\n\n五十二個孩子看著這一幕，誰都沒有動。\n\n「就是這樣。」小筠的聲音很輕，「鏡子，把『那天』撕成了兩半。」\n\n「不是鏡子撕的。」晴晴說，「是那天，本來就有兩種可能。」\n\n就在這時，鏡面中央的裂縫，開始擴大。\n\n「喀啦——」\n\n一道裂紋，從鏡面中央往兩邊蔓延，像閃電，又像一棵正在生長的樹。\n\n裂紋爬出鏡框，爬進牆裡，爬上天花板。\n\n「往後退！」小陽大喊。\n\n孩子們連連後退。\n\n裂紋爬過的地方，世界在「換畫面」：禮堂的地板一下是木頭的，一下是水泥的；觀眾席一下有椅子，一下是空的。\n\n「世界在重疊……不，是在互相擠！」阿達抱住頭。\n\n兩個世界的畫面，像兩卷膠捲，疊在一起，快速地切換。\n\n「它撐不住了。」B 林澈盯著鏡子，「鏡子要裂開了！」\n\n「不會的。」林澈忽然說。\n\n他往前走了一步。\n\n「林澈！」晴晴拉住他的袖子。\n\n「它不會裂。」林澈看著鏡子，聲音很穩，「它只是想讓我們看清楚。」\n\n他繼續往前走。\n\n裂紋在他腳下，忽然停了。\n\n禮堂裡的「換畫面」，也慢慢停了下來。\n\n就像暴風雨，突然被按了暫停。\n\n「你們看。」林澈說。\n\n鏡子裡的兩個畫面，還在。左邊的林澈垂著頭，右邊的林澈笑著。\n\n可是，裂紋不再擴大。\n\n「鏡子在等。」小筠走過來，眼鏡反著光，「它在等林澈。」\n\n「等我？」\n\n「等你看完這兩種可能。」小筠說，「然後，做出選擇。」\n\n「什麼選擇？」阿達問。\n\n「不是選擇哪一個。」小筠搖頭，「是……能不能，同時接受兩個。」\n\n孩子們安靜下來。\n\n林澈站在鏡子前，離鏡面只剩一步。\n\n左邊的自己，垂著頭。右邊的自己，笑著。\n\n兩個都是他。兩個，都不是完整的他。\n\n「我懂了。」林澈輕聲說。\n\n他伸出手，慢慢地，碰向鏡面。\n\n就在指尖碰到鏡面的瞬間——\n\n畫面，像水一樣，盪開了。\n\n林澈的手指，沒入了鏡面。\n\n沒有痛。涼涼的。像伸進一池溫水。\n\n「進去嗎？」B 林澈問。\n\n林澈回頭，看了一眼五十二個孩子。\n\n「不是只有我。」他說，「是我們。」\n\n小陽第一個反應過來，他大喊：「大家手牽手！」\n\n五十二個孩子，在鏡子前，牽起彼此的手。\n\n平常，鏡子一次只能讓八個人通過。可是今晚，鏡子沒有拒絕任何人。\n\n排在最前面的，是兩個林澈。左邊是 A 林澈，右邊是 B 林澈。\n\n他們兩個，同時伸出另一隻手，按在鏡面上。\n\n銀白色的光，從鏡面湧出來，把五十二個人，一個一個地，吞了進去。\n\n世界，變成一片銀白色。\n\n然後——\n\n陽光。\n\n很刺眼的陽光。\n\n林澈張開眼睛。\n\n他站在操場上。九月開學的操場。\n\n天空藍得發亮。海風裡，有草的味道。\n\n五十二個孩子站在他身後，全都愣住了。\n\n「這裡是……」阿達的聲音在抖，「那天？」\n\n「那天。」晴晴點頭。\n\n操場上，六年一班的隊伍正排著。孩子們低著頭，你看我，我看你。\n\n那個劉老師，就站在隊伍前面。\n\n他穿著體育服，脖子上掛著哨子。他看起來，跟現在沒什麼兩樣——也許，年輕一點點。\n\n「老師！」阿達想衝過去。\n\n「等等！」B 林澈攔住他。\n\n阿達的手，從劉老師的身體裡，穿了過去。\n\n像穿過一團光。\n\n孩子們全都安靜了。\n\n「我們……摸不到他們？」小筠的聲音發緊。\n\n「摸不到。」B 林澈說，「這只是鏡子裡的『那天』。是記憶，不是真的。」\n\n就在這時，畫面裡，小小的林澈，慢慢舉起了半隻手。\n\n劉老師看到了。\n\n他走了過來。一步，兩步，三步。\n\n五十二個孩子，全都屏住了呼吸。\n\n劉老師張開了嘴——\n\n而下一秒，整個操場，忽然震了一下。\n\n天空像電視螢幕一樣，閃出一條條雜訊。\n\n「怎麼了？！」孩子們驚叫。\n\n畫面裡的世界，開始在「兩種可能」之間快速切換：劉老師的嘴，一下要說這句話，一下要說那句話。\n\n「時間，快到了。」B 林澈低聲說，「外面的世界，正在等我們。」\n\n他低頭看手錶——可是手錶的指針，停在原地，一動也不動。\n\n「在這裡，時間是停住的。」小筠說，「停在那句話，說出口之前。」\n\n「我們還有多久？」晴晴問。\n\n小筠搖搖頭：「不知道。也許一瞬間，也許永遠。」\n\n「但我們知道一件事——」她看著大家，「午夜之前，我們必須讓這裡的『林澈』，同時看見兩種可能。」\n\n孩子們看向畫面裡那個小小的林澈。\n\n他舉著半隻手，等著劉老師開口。\n\n就像……在等他們。\n\n外面的世界，已經不知道幾點了。\n\n鏡子裡的時間，靜止在那句話之前。\n\n而真正的戰鬥，才正要開始。\n","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 16 — The Mirror Cracks\n\nThe image in the mirror grew clearer and clearer.\n\nDaytime. September. The playground on the third day of school.\n\nThe sunlight was blindingly bright. The children could even \"smell\" the scene — the smell of grass, the smell of the sea breeze.\n\nFifty-two people crowded in front of the mirror, not one of them speaking.\n\nIn the image, Coach Liu blew his whistle.\n\nThen, everyone saw it.\n\nThe mirror's surface split apart.\n\nThe image in the mirror divided into two halves.\n\nLeft: Coach Liu walked up to little Lin Che, his mouth opening—\n\n\"You're more on the quiet side. For the anchor leg, leave it to the kids who run fast.\"\n\nIn the left image, little Lin Che lowered his head and stepped back.\n\nRight: Coach Liu walked up to little Lin Che, his mouth opening—\n\n\"Don't you want to give it a try? I think you can do it.\"\n\nIn the right image, little Lin Che's eyes lit up and he nodded hard.\n\nThe same second. Two possibilities. One mirror, two worlds.\n\nThe fifty-two children watched this scene, none of them moving.\n\n\"That's it.\" Hsiao-Yun's voice was soft. \"The mirror has torn 'that day' in half.\"\n\n\"It wasn't the mirror that tore it,\" Ching-Ching said. \"That day always had two possibilities.\"\n\nJust then, the crack at the center of the mirror began to widen.\n\n\"Crack—\"\n\nA fracture spread from the center of the mirror to both sides, like lightning, like a growing tree.\n\nThe crack climbed out of the mirror frame, into the wall, up to the ceiling.\n\n\"Get back!\" Xiao-Yang yelled.\n\nThe children scrambled backward.\n\nWherever the crack passed, the world \"changed channels\": the auditorium floor was wood one moment, cement the next; the audience seats had chairs one moment, and were empty the next.\n\n\"The worlds are overlapping... no, they're squeezing each other!\" A-Da clutched his head.\n\nThe images of the two worlds, like two film reels stacked together, switched rapidly.\n\n\"It can't hold on.\" B Lin Che stared at the mirror. \"The mirror is going to crack open!\"\n\n\"It won't,\" Lin Che suddenly said.\n\nHe took a step forward.\n\n\"Lin Che!\" Ching-Ching grabbed his sleeve.\n\n\"It won't crack.\" Lin Che looked at the mirror, his voice steady. \"It just wants us to see clearly.\"\n\nHe kept walking forward.\n\nAt his feet, the cracks suddenly stopped.\n\nThe \"channel changing\" in the auditorium slowly stopped too.\n\nLike a storm that had been paused out of nowhere.\n\n\"Look,\" Lin Che said.\n\nThe two images in the mirror were still there. The Lin Che on the left hung his head; the Lin Che on the right was smiling.\n\nBut the cracks were no longer spreading.\n\n\"The mirror is waiting.\" Hsiao-Yun walked over, her glasses reflecting the light. \"It's waiting for Lin Che.\"\n\n\"For me?\"\n\n\"It's waiting for you to finish watching these two possibilities,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"And then make a choice.\"\n\n\"What choice?\" A-Da asked.\n\n\"It's not about choosing which one.\" Hsiao-Yun shook her head. \"It's... whether you can accept both at the same time.\"\n\nThe children fell quiet.\n\nLin Che stood before the mirror, one step from its surface.\n\nThe him on the left hung his head. The him on the right was smiling.\n\nBoth were him. And neither was the whole of him.\n\n\"I understand now,\" Lin Che said softly.\n\nHe reached out his hand and slowly touched the mirror's surface.\n\nThe instant his fingertip met the glass—\n\nThe image rippled like water.\n\nLin Che's finger sank into the mirror.\n\nNo pain. Cool. Like reaching into a pool of warm water.\n\n\"Shall we go in?\" B Lin Che asked.\n\nLin Che turned and looked at the fifty-two children.\n\n\"It's not just me,\" he said. \"It's us.\"\n\nXiao-Yang was the first to react. He shouted: \"Everyone, hold hands!\"\n\nThe fifty-two children, in front of the mirror, took one another's hands.\n\nNormally, the mirror only let eight people through at a time. But tonight, the mirror refused no one.\n\nAt the very front stood the two Lin Ches. A Lin Che on the left, B Lin Che on the right.\n\nThey stretched out their other hands at the same time and pressed them against the mirror's surface.\n\nSilvery-white light surged from the mirror, swallowing the fifty-two children one by one.\n\nThe world turned a single silvery-white.\n\nThen—\n\nSunshine.\n\nBlinding sunshine.\n\nLin Che opened his eyes.\n\nHe was standing on a playground. The playground of a September, the start of a school year.\n\nThe sky was brilliantly blue. In the sea breeze was the smell of grass.\n\nThe fifty-two children stood behind him, all frozen in shock.\n\n\"This place is...\" A-Da's voice trembled. \"That day?\"\n\n\"That day,\" Ching-Ching nodded.\n\nOn the playground, the Class 6-1 line was formed. Children with their heads down, glancing at one another.\n\nThat Coach Liu stood at the front of the line.\n\nHe wore his PE uniform, a whistle around his neck. He looked just like the present day — maybe a little younger.\n\n\"Teacher!\" A-Da tried to run over.\n\n\"Wait!\" B Lin Che stopped him.\n\nA-Da's hand passed right through Coach Liu's body.\n\nLike passing through a mass of light.\n\nThe children all went quiet.\n\n\"We... can't touch them?\" Hsiao-Yun's voice tightened.\n\n\"We can't.\" B Lin Che said. \"This is just 'that day' inside the mirror. A memory, not reality.\"\n\nJust then, in the scene, little Lin Che slowly raised his hand halfway.\n\nCoach Liu saw him.\n\nHe walked over. One step, two steps, three steps.\n\nAll fifty-two children held their breath.\n\nCoach Liu opened his mouth—\n\nAnd the next second, the entire playground trembled.\n\nThe sky flickered with static, like a TV screen.\n\n\"What's happening?!\" the children cried out.\n\nThe world in the scene began switching rapidly between the \"two possibilities\": Coach Liu's mouth now about to say one thing, now about to say the other.\n\n\"Time is running out.\" B Lin Che said quietly. \"The world outside is waiting for us.\"\n\nHe looked down at his watch — but the hands of his watch stayed frozen in place.\n\n\"Here, time is stopped,\" Hsiao-Yun said. \"Stopped right before that sentence was spoken.\"\n\n\"How much time do we have?\" Ching-Ching asked.\n\nHsiao-Yun shook her head: \"I don't know. Maybe an instant. Maybe forever.\"\n\n\"But we know one thing—\" She looked at everyone. \"Before midnight, we have to make the 'Lin Che' here see both possibilities at the same time.\"\n\nThe children looked at the little Lin Che in the scene.\n\nHe held his hand halfway up, waiting for Coach Liu to speak.\n\nAs if... waiting for them.\n\nWho knew what time it was now, in the outside world.\n\nThe time inside the mirror stood frozen before that sentence.\n\nAnd the real battle was only just beginning.\n"}];
